window.SIGNIN_CHAPTERS=(window.SIGNIN_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":26,"title":"Chapter 26: Boycott the Owner","paragraphs":["The following morning, Jude woke up in the master stateroom of the ocean liner.","Beyond the window, the Caribbean Sea stretched toward the horizon.","Jude sat up and stretched. During the previous night’s gathering, several models and actresses had approached him, but he had turned them away.","He had little interest in casual distractions when the system interface remained in the corner of his field of view.","The confrontation on the beach had yielded two daily sign-ins alongside a Platinum Reward Box.","\"System,\" Jude said internally. \"Run both sign-ins. Then open the Platinum Reward Box.\"","[Executing Money Sign-Ins...]","[Sign-In 1 Successful! Reward: $45,000,000 USD.]","[Sign-In 2 Successful! Reward: $55,000,000 USD.]","His phone buzzed on the side table as one hundred million dollars routed into his offshore accounts.","[Opening Platinum System Reward Box...]","[Calculating RNG...]","[Host has acquired three rewards:","[Acquired Skill: Boundless Vitality (Passive).]","[Acquired Asset: $100,000,000 USD Black Card (Restricted: Sapphire Cove Maintenance).]","[Acquired Asset: 100% Exclusive Management Contract (Entity: ’Stellar’).]","Jude paused to review the details.","The passive skill, *Boundless Vitality*, was substantial...","The description indicated that it eliminated the necessity of sleep and cleared mental fatigue.","It removed the ordinary limits of an executive, enabling him to oversee his enterprises without suffering burnout.","The Black Card resolved practical matters.","Managing an island territory and a fleet of vessels required continuous expenditures for upkeep, security, and staff payroll.","The card served as an automated operating fund specifically set aside to cover the running costs of Sapphire Cove.","The third reward caught Jude’s attention...","’Stellar’ was the leading pop group in the domestic market.","The four-member group was an established cultural brand, driving major revenue through tours, merchandise, and commercial endorsements.","Jude opened the contract within his system storage.","Rather than granting a standard share of royalty revenue, it gave him full management control over the group’s professional output and career direction.","Apex Media Group held several corporate subsidiaries, including a music label based in the capital.","Holding direct management authority over the most profitable pop act meant he needed to inspect that branch of the company firsthand.","Spending additional days resting on the coast held little appeal. He preferred active control over passive leisure.","Jude dressed in a charcoal suit and walked out onto the main deck. He found Seraphina Frost holding a drink near the pool.","\"Seraphina,\" Jude said. \"I am returning to the mainland. You are in charge of the event for the rest of the week. Ensure the executives and talent have everything they require.\"","Seraphina set her glass down and stood up. \"You are leaving, Mr. Lawson? The gathering only just began.\"","\"The event is for the staff,\" Jude said. \"I have corporate business to attend to. Tell the crew to prepare the aircraft.\"","Within two hours, Jude was airborne, flying back toward the mainland.","During the flight, he contacted Victoria over a secure channel to ensure the paperwork for the management contract was integrated into Apex Media’s corporate structure.","By afternoon, Jude’s car stopped before the offices of Apex Records... a sixty-story tower of glass situated in the center of the entertainment district.","Rather than notifying the label’s management team to arrange a formal reception, Jude told his driver to remain outside. He chose to enter unannounced to see how the branch operated during ordinary hours, without the staff preparing a display for the owner.","Jude walked through the front doors.","Inside the entrance hall, a wave of noise met him immediately.","The reception floor was crowded. Several hundred young people had gathered across the lobby, blocking the security barriers and the central elevator banks. They carried illuminated signs, light sticks, and promotional boards depicting the four members of *Stellar*.","\"CHLOE! MIA! STELLAR FOREVER!\" a group shouted, holding their signs above the crowd.","Security staff stood near the barriers, trying to keep the crowd back from the inner elevators. Jude observed the room, then moved along the outer perimeter toward the private elevator bank along the far wall.","Before he took five paces, a man in a *Stellar* jacket stepped into his path and shoved him back.","\"Back off, suit,\" the man said. \"No cutting the line. We have been waiting here since four in the morning for the press conference.\"","Jude regained his balance and kept his expression steady. \"I am not here for the press conference. I am heading to the elevators.\"","\"Nobody uses the elevators,\" a woman standing near him said, holding a light stick toward him. \"Not until Apex Records gives us an answer. We are protesting.\"","\"Protesting what?\" Jude asked.","\"You must work for the corporate office,\" the man said. \"Apex Records cannot handle this release. It is a secondary label that has no business managing Stellar’s debut studio album.\"","\"We saw the financial reports,\" another person shouted from the group. \"Apex Media was bought out by an investor who knows nothing about music production. He is going to cut the recording budget and derail the release.\"","Others joined in, taking up the words until a chant echoed through the building.","\"BOYCOTT THE OWNER! SAVE STELLAR!\"","The crowd believed the recent corporate acquisition meant the project would be stripped of capital and creative support...","Jude stood amid the noise, looking at the display screens above the barriers. The monitors showed a countdown timer leading to the scheduled media briefing.","He had arrived to inspect the music division’s operations, only to find the company dealing with a public dispute focused on his purchase of the parent firm.","Jude looked back toward the security gates.","If the public believed Apex Records lacked the capital and scale to manage the production, the upcoming briefing would clarify the matter without ambiguity...","Before Jude could step forward to address the lobby security, a commotion erupted outside the doors of the skyscraper.","A transport SUV with tinted windows had attempted to pull up to the curb.","As the vehicle slowed, an older man in a jacket leaped out from the crowd and threw himself onto the hood of the SUV.","The man screamed, clutching his leg and rolling around as if he had been struck at speed."]},{"number":27,"title":"Chapter 27: The Ambush","paragraphs":["The vehicle slammed on its brakes. The mob of fans swarmed the SUV, blocking it in.","Jude, with his senses from the Boundless Vitality skill, noticed something wrong.","While the fans were banging on the windows and protesting, four men wearing jackets and surgical masks shoved their way through the crowd.","The four men reached the passenger doors of the SUV. One of them pulled a baton from his jacket, smashing the window.","Another reached inside, grabbing the arm of Lyla, the lead singer of Stellar, attempting to drag her out of the vehicle.","Jude grabbed the nearest man by the collar of his jacket, lifting the thug off his feet, and hurled him backward into a planter. The impact knocked the man out.","The leader of the group, a man wearing mirrored sunglasses, spun around, swinging his baton at Jude’s head.","Jude ducked, the baton whistling inches over his hair.","Jude drove his knee upward into the man’s ribs.","The crack of bone echoed over the screams of the crowd.","As the leader collapsed, Jude planted a shoe onto the side of the man’s head, pinning his skull against the asphalt.","The remaining two thugs froze, looking at Jude standing over their leader. In less than five seconds, a man in a tailored suit had dismantled their ambush.","\"If either of you move a single muscle, I will crush his skull,\" Jude said.","Jude applied a fraction of his weight onto his heel. The man under his shoe let out a shriek as the pressure against his temple became unbearable.","\"Now,\" Jude said, looking down at the leader. \"I am only going to ask this once. Idiots usually don’t get a second chance to answer me. Who is your boss?\"","The man in the sunglasses clawed at the asphalt.","\"Wait! I’ll talk!\" the leader wheezed. \"We’re just contractors! The guy who paid us is Silas Grey!\"","\"Silas Grey,\" Jude repeated, his eyes narrowing. He looked past the shattered window of the SUV, where Lyla was huddled in the backseat. \"Do you know him, Lyla?\"","Lyla shook her head. \"N-no, I’ve never heard of him.\"","\"We don’t know who the ultimate client is!\" the leader groaned, his face grinding against the pavement. \"Silas just gives the orders! But you don’t want to mess with him! He runs the underground fixer network in this city. Let us go, and I’ll tell him you’re off-limits!\"","Jude chuckled. \"You think I’m going to let you go? Get up. You and your men are going to take me directly to Silas Grey.\"","Jude lifted his foot. The leader scrambled backward, gasping for air and clutching his ribs.","He nodded, but a glint flashed behind his mirrored sunglasses.","If this man wanted to walk into Silas Grey’s headquarters, he was signing his own death warrant!","\"Mr. Lawson?\" Lyla’s manager whispered from the driver’s seat, recognizing Jude from the corporate memos. \"Should I call the police?\"","\"Get her inside the building,\" Jude commanded. \"The lobby is secure.\"","Jude turned his attention to the hood of the SUV. The older man who had faked the accident had stopped his groaning. Realizing the kidnapping had failed, the man tried to slide off the hood and disappear into the crowd.","\"Hold it right there,\" Jude said, stepping into his path.","The old man froze, holding up his hands. \"I don’t know them! I was just crossing the street! Your driver hit me!\"","\"My driver was stationary when you threw yourself onto the hood,\" Jude said, pointing to the red recording light of the SUV’s dashcam. \"How much did Silas Grey pay you to orchestrate the blockade?\"","The man’s face went pale. \"N-nothing! I didn’t take any money!\"","Jude held out his hand. \"Give me your identification. Now.\"","The con artist pulled out his wallet and handed over his driver’s license.","Jude pulled out his phone and snapped a photo of the ID card.","\"Your face and your actions are recorded on a dashboard camera,\" Jude said. \"You accepted a bribe to facilitate the kidnapping of a corporate asset. My legal team at Vance & Sterling will ensure you are charged with federal conspiracy. You are looking at a minimum of ten years in a maximum-security prison.\"","The con artist’s knees buckled. He collapsed onto the asphalt, grabbing at Jude’s pant leg. \"Please! I didn’t know they were going to kidnap her! They just told me to stop the car! I beg you, spare me!\"","\"Tell it to the federal judge,\" Jude said, grabbing the man by the collar of his jacket. Jude lifted the man off his feet and threw him onto the sidewalk.","The con artist landed hard, sobbing.","Jude turned to the thugs, who were limping toward an unmarked gray van parked near the curb.","\"Get in,\" Jude ordered, sliding into the back of the van. \"Drive.\"","...","Thirty minutes away, in an abandoned warehouse district on the edge of the city, a man wearing a gold chain sat at a table.","This was Silas Grey...","He was an underground fixer, specializing in corporate sabotage and paparazzi extortion.","He was smoking a Cuban cigar, his phone pressed to his ear.","\"Relax, Pierce,\" Silas said, blowing smoke toward the ceiling. \"I already have a team on the ground outside Apex Records. They are securing the girl as we speak. She won’t be attending any press conferences today.\"","On the other end of the line, Donovan Pierce let out a laugh.","\"Excellent work, Silas,\" Donovan said.","Donovan had been humiliated at the private airport earlier that morning.","He could not attack Jude’s billions directly, but he could sabotage Jude’s newly acquired assets.","\"Once you have her secured, I want you to force her to sign a contract termination. We are going to bleed Apex Media dry.\"","Silas tapped ash onto the floor. \"Forcing an idol to break a contract is tricky, Pierce. I’m going to need double my rate for the legal fallout.\"","Donovan cursed under his breath. Silas was greedy, but Donovan was desperate for revenge.","\"Fine,\" Donovan hissed. \"But if I’m paying double, I want her ruined. Don’t just make her sign the papers. Stage a scandal. Take photos of her in a compromising position.\"","Silas chuckled. \"You’re a sick man, Pierce. But I like your style.\"","\"Stellar’s image is built entirely on their reputation,\" Donovan sneered. \"Lyla is the golden child. If you leak photos of her to the tabloids, her brand dies. Apex Records will lose a hundred-million-dollar IP overnight.\"","\"Consider it done,\" Silas grinned, taking a drag of his cigar. \"My men should be pulling up any minute now.\""]},{"number":28,"title":"Chapter 28: True Love","paragraphs":["The doors of the warehouse rolled open The van pulled into the interior and squealed to a halt.","Silas Grey stood up from his table, a grin spreading across his face. He held his phone up to his ear. \"They’re here, Pierce. I’ll call you back when I have the photos.\"","Silas walked over to the back of the van, expecting his men to drag out a pop star.","Instead, the rear doors swung open, and the four thugs tumbled out onto the floor, clutching their ribs.","Silas froze.","Stepping out of the darkness of the van was Jude Lawson.","\"What the hell is this?!\" Silas roared, reaching for the pistol holstered at his hip.","He didn’t even get his hand on the grip. Jude closed the distance with speed.","Jude’s hand shot out, clamping around Silas’s throat, and slammed the fixer backward onto the table.","The phone Silas had been holding clattered onto the surface, the speakerphone still engaged.","\"Silas?\" Donovan Pierce’s voice crackled through the phone speaker. \"What’s going on? Do you have her?\"","Jude kept Silas pinned by the throat with one hand, picking up the phone with the other.","\"Silas is a bit tied up right now, Donovan,\" Jude said.","There was a dead silence on the other end of the line.","\"Lawson?!\" Donovan gasped. \"How... how did you find that number?!\"","\"You really don’t learn, do you?\" Jude chuckled. \"You failed at the private airport, and you failed here. Trying to kidnap my talent is a desperate move.\"","Donovan realized he was caught, but his arrogance refused to let him back down. \"It doesn’t matter, Lawson! Apex Records is absolute garbage! The fans are already boycotting you! Without my studio’s backing, Stellar is going to bleed market value until they jump ship. Your little music division is going to crash and burn!\"","Jude laughed. \"Donovan, I don’t care about market value. If a company burns money, I simply print more. In fact, I am personally injecting two hundred million dollars into Stellar’s contract renewal today. Can your studio match a two-hundred-million-dollar retainer?\"","Donovan’s breath hitched.","\"You’re a maniac!\" Donovan shrieked, his voice cracking before he slammed the phone down, disconnecting the call.","Jude tossed the phone onto the floor, crushing it under his shoe.","He looked down at Silas, who was trembling against the table.","\"The police are about three minutes away,\" Jude said coldly, releasing the fixer’s throat. \"I suggest you have a good lawyer.\"","[Ding!]","[Mission Completed: Crush the Opponent’s Conspiracy.]","[Reward: +1 Money Sign-In, +1 Platinum System Reward Box!]","Jude ignored the thugs and walked out of the warehouse, hailing a sedan to take him back to the Apex Records skyscraper.","When Jude arrived at the music division’s headquarters, the lobby was secured. The crowd of protesting fans was being held back behind barricades by the police.","Jude bypassed the chaos and entered the secured VIP glass atrium on the ground floor.","Sitting on the sofas was Lyla. Sitting next to her, holding her hand, was Mia. Their manager was pacing in the background.","When Jude walked in, Lyla immediately stood up.","\"Mr. Lawson,\" Lyla breathed, tears welling up in her eyes. \"Thank you. If you hadn’t been there...\"","\"It’s handled,\" Jude said, offering a smile. He turned to the manager. \"I assume you have the preliminary contracts for their upcoming renewal cycle?\"","The manager blinked. \"Y-yes, sir. We were preparing a standard two-year extension. Ten million a year for the group.\"","\"Shred it,\" Jude commanded.","The manager froze. \"Sir?\"","\"I want a new contract drafted immediately,\" Jude said, pulling out a pen from his jacket pocket. \"A one-year commitment. And the base salary will be one hundred million dollars for Lyla, and one hundred million dollars for Mia. Furthermore, the contract strictly prohibits any transfer negotiations with Pierce Studios.\"","Lyla and Mia gasped simultaneously. The manager nearly dropped his briefcase...","\"One... one hundred million?\" Mia stammered, her face flushing crimson. \"Each?!\"","\"Mr. Lawson, I feel like that is far too much,\" Lyla protested. \"We are popular, yes, but we aren’t worth a hundred million dollars a year. That kind of budget is unheard of for a single album cycle.\"","Jude looked at the two girls. \"I keep my word. A hundred million is exactly what you are worth to this company. If you think it’s too much, then work hard, get in the studio, and help me earn my investment back.\"","Lyla and Mia looked at each other.","They were used to ruthless corporate executives trying to squeeze every penny out of them. But the billionaire standing in front of them had just risked his life to save them, and was now offering them a financial safety net that would set their families up for generations!","*He must be our biggest fan,* Lyla thought, her cheeks burning hot. *He bought the entire company and fought off thugs just to protect us!*","Lyla and Mia stepped forward.","Before Jude could even register their movement, the two pop stars leaned in from opposite sides and pressed their lips against his cheeks.","\"Thank you, boss,\" Lyla whispered, her voice sweet and genuine. \"We won’t let you down.\"","\"We will work so hard for you,\" Mia added, blushing as she pulled back.","Outside the walls of the VIP atrium, the crowd of protesting fans witnessed the entire exchange.","The fans who had been screaming for Apex Records to burn down suddenly went dead silent.","They stared through the glass, watching their idols kiss the cheeks of the \"evil corporate billionaire.\"","A second later, the crowd lost their minds.","\"NOOO!\" a hardcore fan screamed. \"MY QUEEN! IT CAN’T BE TRUE!\"","\"He bought their love!\" another fan shrieked. \"I’m going to jump off a bridge! This is the worst day of my life!\"","Jude chuckled, reaching up to touch his cheek.","It was obvious the two girls had completely misunderstood his intentions, assuming this was an romantic rescue mission...","Having the loyalty of the nation’s biggest pop stars was exactly what he needed to secure his new music division.","Lyla and Mia stayed close to Jude’s side, whispering excitedly to each other as he led them toward the private executive elevator.","\"I’ve never even seen him in the celebrity magazines,\" Mia whispered, stealing a glance at Jude’s profile. \"How much is he actually worth?\"","\"I read that the true billionaires never appear on the rich lists,\" Lyla whispered back, her eyes shining with admiration. \"He must be one of those hidden titans. We are so lucky.\"","The elevator doors chimed open on the sixtieth floor.","Jude stepped out into the executive suite.","Waiting for him in the central boardroom were the three pillars of Apex Records... Director Vance, Director Chen, and Director Xue.","The executives stood up immediately as Jude entered, their eyes darting between the billionaire and the two idols trailing behind him.","\"Mr. Lawson,\" Director Vance said, bowing his head. \"It is an honor. We are at your disposal.\""]},{"number":29,"title":"Chapter 29: Celebration","paragraphs":["Jude bypassed the pleasantries, walking straight to the head of the boardroom table.","He took a seat in the executive chair, gesturing for the three directors to sit.","Lyla and Mia quietly took seats near the corner, trying to make themselves as small as possible in the presence of the label’s highest authorities.","\"Let’s cut right to the operational metrics,\" Jude said. \"I want a blunt assessment of the music division’s current talent roster and its operating capital.\"","Director Vance adjusted his tie. \"Of course, Mr. Lawson. I won’t sugarcoat it. Currently, Apex Records is running a very lean roster. We have two solid B-list solo artists who generate consistent streaming revenue. Beyond them, we have about forty indie and tertiary acts on short-term developmental contracts.\"","\"And the financials?\" Jude asked.","\"We have several stadium tours in production,\" Director Xue chimed in, opening a ledger. \"The upfront investment for staging, marketing, and logistics is draining our reserves. Last fiscal year, despite grossing a respectable amount, the division’s actual net profit was a meager forty million dollars.\"","For a localized studio, it would be a success. But for the music division of a multi-billion-dollar media conglomerate, it was essentially pocket change...","Director Chen, the oldest of the three executives, let out a sigh and looked toward Lyla and Mia.","\"Mr. Lawson, forgive me for speaking out of turn,\" Director Chen began carefully. \"But your assistant informed us downstairs that you authorized a two-hundred-million-dollar contract renewal for Stellar. Given our forty-million-dollar net profit... that contract is financially ruinous. We simply do not have the operating capital to absorb a two-hundred-million-dollar salary payout without bankrupting the entire division’s ledger.\"","Lyla and Mia visibly flinched.","Facing the judgment of the veteran directors, the two pop stars lowered their heads, feeling out of place.","They were artists, not corporate strategists...","In the eyes of the board, they were suddenly a massive financial liability.","Mia chewed her bottom lip nervously, looking over at Jude with a pleading expression.","Jude looked at Director Chen. \"If the current operating capital is insufficient to support my artists, Director Chen, then the solution is simple,\" Jude stated smoothly. \"I will rewrite the ledger.\"","The three directors stared at him.","\"I am officially authorizing a personal capital injection into Apex Records,\" Jude announced, leaning back in his chair. \"I will provide an additional one billion dollars annually, entirely dedicated to roster development and studio expansion. Do you possess the administrative capability to manage a billion-dollar development fund, or do I need to find a new board of directors?\"","The boardroom fell into silence.","Director Vance stared at Jude as if the young man had just offered to personally fund a space program.","\"One... one billion dollars?\" Director Xue stammered. \"Annually?!\"","\"Your base corporate valuation was just over two billion when I bought the conglomerate,\" Jude said, pulling out his smartphone. \"Adding a billion in liquid capital gives you the leverage to dominate the industry.\"","Jude accessed his offshore accounts through his encrypted interface. With a few taps on the screen, he routed five hundred million dollars straight into Apex Records’ corporate account as a six-month down payment.","Ten seconds later, the tablet sitting in front of Director Chen chimed.","The director looked down at the banking notification. His face went pale. The influx of capital had already cleared.","\"It’s... it’s here,\" Director Chen whispered in awe.","Director Vance let out a booming laugh, his demeanor shifting from cautious to sycophantic.","\"Mr. Lawson, your liquidity is terrifying!\" Director Vance praised. \"With a billion-dollar war chest, all of our logistical bottlenecks vanish overnight! We can outbid every major label on the continent!\"","Director Chen immediately turned toward Lyla and Mia, offering them an apologetic smile.","\"I completely retract my previous statement,\" Director Chen said. \"Lyla, Mia, you two are generational talents. You are the core of this label’s future. With Mr. Lawson’s funding, we will launch a global marketing campaign that will make your previous tours look like local theater.\"","Lyla and Mia let out a sigh of relief. They looked at Jude with profound loyalty.","He hadn’t just protected their contract; he had bent the board of directors to his will just to secure their future!","Jude slipped his phone back into his pocket.","\"Since the financial restructuring is settled,\" Director Vance said, standing up. \"I believe it is imperative that we formally introduce you to the rest of the roster, Mr. Lawson. The artists need to see the man who is about to revolutionize their careers.\"","Ten minutes later, Director Vance had called an assembly in the label’s acoustic training hall.","Over fifty signed artists, ranging from indie producers to established pop vocalists, had been pulled from their recording booths and dance rehearsals.","Standing near the front row of the assembly were the label’s two most prominent mid-tier artists...","A platinum-selling R&B vocalist named Orion, and a popular electro-pop singer named Elena.","\"If the rumors are true, this is the best thing that could have happened to us,\" Orion said confidently, adjusting his jacket. \"Apex Records was bleeding cash on those stadium tours. We needed a billionaire to step in.\"","\"Quiet,\" Elena hissed, nodding toward the doors at the back of the hall. \"They’re coming.\"","The doors swung open.","Jude walked into the acoustic training hall, flanked by the three senior directors and the two idols of Stellar.","Every artist in the hall stared at Jude in shock. They had expected a gray-haired, Wall Street tycoon in a stuffy suit. Instead, they were looking at a handsome young man.","\"My god, he’s so young,\" Elena whispered, her eyes wide.","Director Vance stepped up to the microphone stand at the center of the room.","\"Ladies and gentlemen, it is my honor to introduce you to the sole owner of Apex Records, Mr. Jude Lawson,\"","\"And I am thrilled to announce that Mr. Lawson has just authorized an annual, one-billion-dollar capital injection into this label’s development fund!\"","The training hall exploded.","It was a tidal wave of pure cheering...","Dancers, singers, and producers screamed in excitement.","A billion dollars meant endless recording budgets, massive promotional tours, and top-tier production equipment...","The new boss hadn’t come to slash their contracts; he had come to elevate them all to superstardom!","Orion and Elena stepped forward from the front row.","\"Mr. Lawson, it is an honor,\" Orion said smoothly, offering a bow. \"Your vision for this label is incredible. We are at your service.\"","\"We would love to properly celebrate your arrival, Mr. Lawson,\" Elena added, flashing a smile as she stepped closer. \"Orion and I would be honored to host a welcome banquet for you tonight at the Obsidian Grand. The entire senior roster will be there to celebrate the new era of Apex Records.\"","The surrounding artists cheered their agreement, desperate for a chance to network with the billionaire.","Jude looked at the eager, expectant faces of his newly acquired talent.","He had spent the morning dismantling a kidnapping and restructuring a corporation...","A celebration at the city’s most exclusive hotel sounded like the perfect way to conclude the day.","\"I accept,\" Jude said. \"Set it up.\""]},{"number":30,"title":"Chapter 30: The Chairman","paragraphs":["The Diamond Ballroom at the Obsidian Grand Hotel was reserved for Apex Records.","By nine o’clock that evening, the hall was filled with the label’s top artists, producers, and executives.","Jude sat at the center of the VIP table, nursing a glass of bourbon.","\"Mr. Lawson, to celebrate your arrival, we thought we should demonstrate exactly what kind of talent you’ve invested in,\" Elena announced, stepping into the open space in front of the VIP table.","Elena was wearing a backless crimson dress. As the ballroom’s acoustic band began to play a slow bassline, Elena launched into a choreographed dance routine.","She was a professional through and through, but it was obvious to everyone in the room that this was a targeted performance...","Every single time Elena twirled or struck a pose, her eyes locked onto Jude, flashing him lingering looks.","It was a blatant attempt to seduce the new billionaire owner.","Sitting on the sofa behind Jude, Lyla and Mia watched the performance with narrowing eyes.","\"She is shameless,\" Mia whispered to Lyla, her jaw clenching. \"She’s practically throwing herself at him.\"","Lyla nodded, feeling a spike of jealousy.","Jude had risked his life to save them from thugs earlier that day. He had given them a hundred million dollars each.","In Lyla’s mind, Jude was *their* savior, and she wasn’t about to let an opportunistic pop star steal his attention.","\"We are not letting her outshine us,\" Lyla whispered.","As soon as Elena finished her routine to a round of polite applause, Lyla and Mia immediately stood up, smoothing out their designer dresses.","\"That was beautiful, Elena,\" Lyla said, stepping past the other singer to take the floor. \"But we would also like to offer Mr. Lawson a proper welcome.\"","The ballroom grew quiet as the two most famous idols in the country took their positions.","Lyla and Mia didn’t need a heavy bassline or a sultry dance routine. They signaled the acoustic guitarist, and as a melodic chord filled the room, the two girls began to sing.","Their voices harmonized with perfection. It was an acoustic rendition of their biggest chart-topping hit, but stripped of the studio production, the power of their vocals was undeniable.","Throughout the song, Lyla and Mia kept their gaze locked on Jude, singing the lyrics directly to him.","Jude swirled his bourbon, an amused smile touching his lips.","He could clearly see the competitive tension between the female artists, but watching the nation’s top talent battle for his favor was an entertaining way to spend the evening...","Just as Lyla hit the final high note of the chorus, a crash echoed through the room.","The doors of the Diamond Ballroom were shoved open, slamming against the walls.","The music ground to a halt. The Apex Records artists turned in shock as a tall man in a silver suit marched into the ballroom, flanked by bodyguards and rival executives.","\"Well, isn’t this adorable?\" the man sneered. \"The Wall Street billionaire buys a new toy and immediately sets up a private harem for himself.\"","Director Vance, who was sitting next to Jude, went pale. He leaned in, his voice trembling.","\"Mr. Lawson, that is Derrick Vanguard,\" Director Vance whispered. \"He is the Chairman and majority shareholder of Vanguard Records. They are our fiercest corporate rivals in the city.\"","Derrick Vanguard strutted toward the center of the room, his eyes scanning the crowd with disdain.","When his gaze landed on Elena, a smile spread across his face.","\"Elena, darling,\" Derrick said, extending a hand toward her. \"I told you last month that you belong at a real label. Pack up your things. Vanguard Records is formally offering to buy out your contract right now.\"","Elena frowned, crossing her arms.","\"What kind of future do you think you have here?\" Derrick laughed, gesturing toward Jude. \"Your new boss is an absolute layman. He’s a clueless finance suit who doesn’t know the first thing about the music industry. I heard the rumors, Lawson! You authorized two hundred million dollars for Stellar?!\"","Derrick pointed at Lyla and Mia, scoffing loudly. \"Two hundred million for two girls whose brand is already stalling! It’s the most amateur business decision I’ve ever seen!\"","Lyla flinched, her hands balling into fists.","Elena didn’t hesitate. She glared at Derrick and took three steps backward, intentionally placing herself behind Jude’s chair.","\"I respectfully decline your offer, Mr. Vanguard,\" Elena said. \"I am happy with Apex Records.\"","Derrick’s smug smile faltered, his eyes flashing with irritation at the public rejection. But he quickly recovered, letting out a sigh.","\"Suit yourselves,\" Derrick boasted, turning to address the entire ballroom of Apex artists. \"I was trying to throw you a lifeline before your company sinks. Because as of an hour ago, Vanguard Records has officially acquired exclusive, lifetime management rights to *The Velvet 32*.\"","A collective gasp echoed through the Diamond Ballroom.","Even Director Vance let out a choked breath, his hands shaking as he gripped the edge of the VIP table.","\"The Velvet 32?\" Orion whispered, staring at Derrick in disbelief. \"That’s impossible. They are an independent supergroup!\"","Derrick fed off the shock in the room. \"Not anymore! We bought them out completely!\"","The Velvet 32 was an absolute juggernaut in the entertainment industry...","They were a massive supergroup consisting of thirty-two multi-talented performers.","They dominated television ratings, social media metrics, and streaming charts. Their global fanbase was estimated at over forty million people!","\"Do you understand what this means, Lawson?\" Derrick sneered, looking down at Jude. \"With the Velvet 32 under my control, Vanguard Records holds a monopoly over the pop market. The volume of their fanbase allows me to dictate industry trends. I can make anyone a star, and I can crush anyone who stands in my way!\"","Several of the indie artists and backup dancers in the back of the room exchanged nervous glances.","The power to leverage a forty-million-person fanbase was unprecedented...","Being signed to Vanguard Records suddenly looked like a guaranteed ticket to international fame.","Derrick Vanguard had crashed the party for one specific reason: to break the Apex Records roster and assert his dominance over the new billionaire.","Jude remained seated. He took a sip of his bourbon.","Before Jude could respond to the Chairman, a familiar chime rang clearly in his mind.","[Ding!]","[Continuous Mission Triggered: Unrivaled Stardom.]","[Objective: A rival label is attempting to leverage a forty-million-fan supergroup to undermine your corporate authority and poach your talent. Show them that their supergroup is nothing but a localized fad. Prove the absolute dominance of your own assets.]","[Reward: +1 Money Sign-In, +1 Platinum System Reward Box!]","Jude lowered his glass. A smile slowly crept across his face.","The system wanted him to crush Derrick Vanguard’s newly acquired pride and joy. And Jude knew exactly how to do it."]},{"number":31,"title":"Chapter 31: Supergroup","paragraphs":["\"A massive supergroup, Derrick?\" Jude said. \"What an interesting coincidence. I also happened to acquire a collective recently.\"","Derrick blinked, then threw his head back and let out a laugh.","\"You?\" Derrick mocked, looking around at his executives, who joined in the laughter. \"What did you buy, Lawson? A struggling indie choir from a community college? A washed-up boy band from the nineties?\"","Derrick stepped closer to the VIP table, leaning on the back of an empty chair. \"You clearly don’t understand the capital required to play at this level. I spent two billion dollars to acquire the exclusive management rights to the Velvet 32! It is an asset class that Wall Street suits can’t even comprehend. An entertainment collective of that magnitude is a billion-dollar star-making engine!\"","To him, the Velvet 32 was an unstoppable juggernaut that placed Vanguard Records at the pinnacle of the industry.","Director Vance leaned closer to Jude.","\"Mr. Lawson, you didn’t mention another acquisition during the board meeting,\" Director Vance whispered. \"What team did you buy? A forty-million-fan collective is incredibly difficult to combat in the current media cycle.\"","Orion stepped closer to the table.","\"There’s only one group in the world that can completely eclipse the Velvet 32,\" Orion muttered. \"The Sirens. They are an eighty-eight-member global collective. They have three A-list megastars anchoring the team, and their combined fanbase is pushing eighty million across all platforms.\"","Elena gasped. \"Eighty million? That’s double the Velvet 32. But they are untouchable.\"","Derrick Vanguard’s ears caught Orion’s conversation. He barked out another cruel laugh.","\"The Sirens?\" Derrick scoffed, shaking his head. \"Don’t even dream about it! Vanguard Records offered their parent company three billion dollars last quarter for a fifty-percent stake. You know what they did? They laughed and hung up on me! Nobody in this industry has the capital to acquire The Sirens. They are a sovereign entity in the music world!\"","The Apex Records artists sighed.","If a titan like Derrick Vanguard couldn’t buy his way into The Sirens with three billion dollars, it was an impossible dream...","The Velvet 32 would remain the undisputed kings of the industry.","Jude swirled the amber liquid in his glass, amused by Derrick’s grandstanding.","\"They hung up on you, Derrick?\" Jude asked, a smirk playing on his lips. \"That doesn’t surprise me.\"","\"And why is that, Lawson?\" Derrick challenged, crossing his arms.","\"Because they were waiting for a real offer,\" Jude stated. \"When I dropped a billion dollars into my development fund this afternoon, I also had my acquisitions team execute a hostile buyout of their parent company. I didn’t offer for a fifty-percent stake. I bought them outright.\"","The Diamond Ballroom fell into silence.","The clinking of champagne glasses ceased. The acoustic guitarist in the corner dropped his pick onto the floor, the tiny *click* sounding like a gunshot in the room.","Derrick Vanguard’s smug expression shattered.","The blood drained from his face as his brain tried to process Jude’s claim.","\"You... you bought The Sirens?\" Director Vance choked out.","\"You’re lying!\" Derrick screamed, his voice cracking. \"That is a lie! You did not buy The Sirens! You’re just trying to save face in front of your artists because I humiliated you!\"","Derrick pointed a shaking finger at Jude’s chest. \"I see through you, Lawson! You think you can just drop a name and everyone will bow down to you? If you actually own The Sirens, prove it!\"","\"I don’t need to prove anything to you, Derrick,\" Jude replied.","\"Call them!\" Derrick challenged, his face turning red. \"If you are the sole owner of the eighty-eight-member supergroup, then you have their management on speed dial! Call them right now! Have them walk into this hotel!\"","Derrick was breathing heavily. \"If you can summon The Sirens to this ballroom tonight, I will drop to my knees in front of your entire roster and beg for your forgiveness! But when they don’t show up, I am going to expose you as the fraud you are!\"","Jude raised an eyebrow. \"You want to drop to your knees? By all means, Derrick. Let me facilitate that for you.\"","Without breaking eye contact with the furious CEO, Jude reached into the inner pocket of his jacket and pulled out his smartphone. He scrolled to an encrypted contact list.","He tapped the screen, placing the call on speakerphone and setting the device down on the polished mahogany table.","The phone rang twice before it was picked up.","\"Mr. Lawson!\" a crisp female voice answered. \"This is the Executive Director for The Sirens. It is an honor to speak with you. We received the finalized buyout paperwork this afternoon. The entire collective is at your disposal.\"","The Apex Records artists gasped. Derrick Vanguard’s eyes went wide.","\"Director,\" Jude said calmly. \"I am currently hosting a welcome banquet at the Diamond Ballroom in the Obsidian Grand Hotel. Gather the entire eighty-eight-member team. I want them here immediately.\"","\"Right away, Mr. Lawson!\" the Director replied without hesitation. \"The team is currently at their downtown recording compound. We will load the transport fleet and be at the Obsidian Grand in twenty minutes.\"","Jude tapped the screen, ending the call. He looked up at Derrick, whose face was a mask of horror.","\"Twenty minutes,\" Jude said, taking a sip of his bourbon. \"I suggest you stretch your knees, Derrick. The floor looks quite hard.\"","Derrick stumbled backward. He looked at his rival executives, who were paralyzed with fear.","If Jude Lawson truly owned The Sirens, Vanguard Records was obsolete...","The Velvet 32 was a massive asset, but compared to the global juggernaut of The Sirens, they were practically a garage band.","Derrick turned toward Elena.","\"Elena, listen to me,\" Derrick pleaded, his voice stripped of arrogance. \"This guy is a maniac! He’s going to bankrupt this entire conglomerate! My offer still stands. Walk out of this hotel with me, and I will double your base salary at Vanguard!\"","Elena didn’t look at him. She crossed her arms, her eyes locked on Jude with admiration.","\"I already told you, Mr. Vanguard,\" Elena said. \"I am perfectly happy with my boss.\"","The rest of the Apex Records roster remained silent, watching Derrick panic.","In twenty minutes, the biggest supergroup on the planet was going to walk through the doors..."]},{"number":32,"title":"Chapter 32: Backfire","paragraphs":["Meanwhile, earlier that afternoon across town, inside the executive boardroom of Pierce Studios...","Donovan Pierce was nursing a glass of scotch, a smirk resting on his face. Surrounding him were the studio’s top shareholders and vice presidents.","\"Gentlemen, you can put your concerns regarding Apex Records to rest,\" Donovan announced, raising his glass. \"I have it on good authority that their music division is about to suffer a catastrophic PR disaster. Their lead asset is compromised.\"","\"Are you certain, Donovan?\" a vice president asked cautiously. \"Lawson just injected capital into the conglomerate. If Stellar renews their contracts, Apex will dominate the Q3 charts.\"","\"They aren’t renewing anything,\" Donovan laughed, taking a sip of his scotch. \"Trust me, the girl’s brand is about to be ruined.\"","Donovan felt a rush of satisfaction. Silas Grey was a professional.","By now, the photos were probably being shopped around to the tabloids...","Apex Records was going to burn, and Jude Lawson’s billion-dollar investment would go up in smoke.","\"Prepare a press release,\" Donovan commanded, waving his hand. \"When the scandal breaks, I want Pierce Studios positioned to absorb their sponsorships. It’s a two-birds-one-stone strategy.\"","\"Sir?\"","One of the executives at the end of the table spoke up, his voice trembling.","He was staring at the television mounted on the boardroom wall, which was tuned to a news network.","\"What is it?\" Donovan snapped.","\"I... I don’t think she’s resigning, sir,\" the executive stammered, pointing a finger at the screen.","Donovan frowned and turned his head.","The television screen was broadcasting a live feed from the VIP atrium of Apex Records.","Standing in the center of the room, looking radiant and unharmed, were Lyla and Mia.","The headline banner scrolling across the bottom of the screen read:","BREAKING: APEX RECORDS SECURES STELLAR WITH UNPRECEDENTED $200 MILLION RENEWAL CONTRACT.","On the screen, Lyla was smiling for the cameras, holding up a signed corporate binder.","Donovan Pierce’s eyes bulged out of his head. He spit out a mouthful of scotch, the liquid spraying across the table.","\"What?!\" Donovan shrieked, his voice cracking.","He stared at the screen, his brain short-circuiting.","*How is she standing in that lobby?!* Donovan’s mind screamed. *Wasn’t she supposed to be locked inside Silas Grey’s warehouse?!*","***","Later that night, high above the city in the penthouse suite of the Obsidian Grand...","\"You are actually terrifying when you want to be, Jude,\" Maya’s voice crackled through the phone line. \"I just saw the financial blogs. Derrick Vanguard’s stock is already tanking in aftermarket trading.\"","Jude stood by the windows of his penthouse suite at the top of the Obsidian Grand, looking out over the glittering city skyline.","The banquet had been a legendary success...","When The Sirens had arrived, Derrick Vanguard had fled the hotel.","Jude sighed. \"Tomorrow morning, when I officially sign the integration contracts, Apex Media and Zenith Motors will be unstoppable. Every piece of the board is moving exactly as calculated.\"","Maya laughed, her voice filled with admiration. \"I never doubted you for a second. The way you restructure these massive conglomerates is on another level.\"","\"I appreciate that,\" Jude said, feeling a wave of warmth. \"Speaking of tomorrow, are you still planning to review the new Zenith expansion ledgers in person?\"","\"Absolutely,\" Maya said, her excitement palpable. \"I’ll be at the penthouse first thing in the morning. I need to see exactly how you plan to merge our logistics with Apex’s new talent contracts.\"","\"Perfect,\" Jude smiled. \"I’ll have the blueprints ready. Have a good night, Maya.\"","\"You too, boss,\" she replied, ending the call.","Jude slipped his phone into his pocket.","He had conquered the domestic entertainment market in a single afternoon, and tomorrow would solidify his empire... But for now, he needed to decompress.","He walked over to the digital intercom mounted on the wall and pressed the direct line to the hotel’s head concierge.","\"Mr. Lawson,\" the concierge answered instantly. \"How may we serve you tonight?\"","\"I’ve had a long day,\" Jude said. \"Have the head chef prepare a Wagyu ribeye, seared rare, along with a bone broth. I want it sent up to the penthouse in one hour.\"","\"Consider it done, sir. We will begin preparation immediately.\"","Jude severed the connection and headed toward the master bathroom. He stripped off his suit and stepped into the shower, cranking the temperature dial all the way to cold.","After ten minutes of silence under the freezing spray, Jude stepped out, drying off with a towel.","He bypassed his collection of bespoke suits, opting instead for a pair of dark tactical cargo pants and a fitted black shirt.","Feeling refreshed, Jude made his way down the floating glass staircase to the penthouse’s private screening room.","The theater was a masterpiece of modern design...","Jude sank into the center recliner, picking up the remote. He bypassed the financial news networks and flipped the channel to a live broadcast of an underground mixed martial arts championship.","The arena lights were bright on the screen. The two fighters stepping into the hexagonal cage were a study in contrast.","One was a hulking brawler. The other was a lean striker, built for speed.","\"Ladies and gentlemen!\"","\"Tonight, we witness the ultimate clash of styles for the undisputed title!\"","Jude leaned back, watching intently.","The massive brawler charged forward with brute strength, throwing looping hooks.","But the leaner fighter used his agility to slip under the onslaught, delivering a kick to the back of the giant’s knee.","The crowd on the screen roared as the big man staggered, but he recovered instantly, grabbing the smaller fighter by the waist and slamming him into the canvas with a crash.","Jude winced slightly.","The brawler fought exactly like Donovan Pierce and Derrick Vanguard...","As the match dragged into the later rounds, the lean fighter weathered the storm.","He absorbed the punishment, waited for the giant to overextend, and then struck with surgical precision.","In a stunning reversal, the tactical fighter slipped his hips, wrapped his legs around the giant’s neck, and locked in a triangle choke.","The giant thrashed, using all his remaining strength to break the hold.","A few seconds later, the brawler tapped the mat in defeat.","Jude slowly clapped his hands in the theater, appreciating the victory.","Seeking a change of pace, Jude flipped the channel to a horror film.","The movie opened with a chilling orchestral score. The setting was a Victorian mansion, isolated in a rainstorm. A group of college students arrived at the estate.","Jude watched as the characters began making every illogical decision imaginable.","They willfully ignored the warning signs on the gates. They split up to explore the unlit basement.","When the power was cut, rather than grouping together to secure a perimeter, they wandered into the shadows.","The cinematic tension was supposed to be terrifying. Supernatural entities began picking the students off one by one. But Jude was profoundly annoyed.","After twenty minutes of watching a teenager slowly back into a dark closet while a monster was standing right behind her, Jude couldn’t take it anymore...","He hit the power button, plunging the theater into darkness.","Jude sighed, shaking his head. \"I’ll stick to the financial markets.\"","Sitting in the quiet darkness of the theater, Jude’s mind pivoted away from the screen and back to the true layout of his growing empire.","He closed his eyes, visualizing the blueprints for the new Zenith Motors headquarters he planned to build in the city’s commercial district.","He pictured a towering, sleek monolith of black glass and steel that would overshadow the surrounding corporate skyline.","Jude wouldn’t rely on standard corporate guards. He would contract elite private military firms to secure the perimeter.","He saw himself expanding beyond the domestic borders. With The Sirens under his control, he had a direct pipeline into the global entertainment market.","A sharp knock echoed through the penthouse.","Jude’s eyes snapped open. The food wasn’t due for another thirty minutes, and the concierge always called before sending staff up to the private floor.","\"Who is it?\" Jude called out."]},{"number":33,"title":"Chapter 33: Entertainment Industry","paragraphs":["\"It’s Maya, Jude,\" a voice called through the door. \"And I have Director Vance from Apex Records with me. I apologize for the late intrusion, but we have a time-sensitive emergency.\"","Jude crossed the room and unlocked the door. Maya was standing in the hallway holding a tablet. Beside her, Director Vance looked on the verge of a panic attack.","\"Come in,\" Jude said, gesturing toward the living area of the penthouse. \"What is the emergency?\"","\"It’s the Global Soundwave Network, Mr. Lawson,\" Director Vance explained, following Jude into the room. \"They are the largest international streaming conglomerate in the world. Once a year, they hold a blind digital auction for ten headliner spots across their entire global platform. Winning those spots guarantees international superstardom.\"","Maya set the tablet down on the coffee table. The screen displayed a digital bidding lobby.","\"Derrick Vanguard lodged a bid of two hundred million dollars for the ten spots,\" Maya said. \"The auction closes in three minutes. He’s buying them to lock Apex Records out of the global market. If we lose this auction, our artists won’t get premium placement on any international streaming playlist for a year.\"","Jude looked at the tablet. He could see rival entertainment tycoons creeping the price up.","\"Two hundred million?\" Jude mused. He sat down on the leather sofa. \"Derrick plays far too small.\"","Jude reached out, pulled the tablet toward him, and tapped the digital entry pad.","He didn’t bother calculating a competitive counter-offer. He authorized a bid from his offshore accounts.","He typed in a flat $1,000,000,000.","He hit submit.","The digital auction lobby on the screen instantly froze. The scrolling feed of corporate bids stopped dead.","Director Vance stared at the tablet, his eyes bulging. \"One... one billion dollars?! Even if the ten spots guarantee international fame, the return on investment from streaming revenue won’t even cover thirty percent of that bid! It’s a massive loss!\"","Jude leaned back, unconcerned. \"Director Vance, do I look like a man who cares about a seventy percent deficit on a marketing expense? I don’t care about the return on investment.\"","On the screen, the other representatives were dumbfounded. No one dared to lodge a counter-bid against a billion dollars.","Ten seconds later, the tablet chimed. The network executives at Global Soundwave accepted the bid and locked the auction.","\"They accepted,\" Maya whispered in awe.","[Ding!]","[Continuous Mission Completed: Unrivaled Stardom.]","[Reward: +1 Money Sign-In, +1 Platinum System Reward Box!]","Jude smiled faintly.","He had an omnipotent financial system backing him...","Spending a billion dollars to crush Derrick Vanguard was worth it.","\"Director Vance,\" Jude said, standing up. \"The spots are secured. I will see you at the studio tomorrow morning to finalize the talent allocations.\"","\"Y-yes, Mr. Lawson. Thank you!\" Director Vance bowed and hurried out of the penthouse.","Jude mentally accessed his system interface.","\"System, execute the money sign-in,\" Jude commanded.","[Sign-In Successful! Reward: $60,000,000 USD.]","[Bonus Sign-In Successful! Reward: $50,000,000 USD.]","[Bonus Sign-In Successful! Reward: $150,000,000 USD.]","Jude felt his phone buzz.","Nearly three hundred million dollars had just been deposited into his accounts. He had just spent a billion, and the system had instantly refunded a third of it.","\"Now,\" Jude thought. \"Open the Platinum Reward Box.\"","[Opening Platinum System Reward Box...]","[Congratulations, Host! You have acquired three premium rewards!]","[Acquired Skill: Absolute Discernment (Passive).]","[Acquired Skill: Flawless Oration (Passive).]","[Acquired Assets: Three $100,000,000 USD Corporate Slush Funds (Categories: Digital Media, Luxury Real Estate, Bespoke Assets).]","The *Absolute Discernment* skill was fascinating...","The system detailed that he would now be able to instantly recognize the difference between natural authenticity and artificial enhancement... whether it was a person’s appearance, the structural integrity of a building, or the hidden clauses in a corporate contract. Nothing could be hidden from his gaze!","The *Flawless Oration* skill upgraded his vocal resonance and public speaking abilities.","His words would now naturally command the attention of any audience.","Possessing the ability to dominate a crowded press conference or a hostile shareholder meeting was a powerful weapon...","The three slush funds were the cherry on top. He now had three hundred million dollars earmarked for expansion.","...","The following morning, Jude arrived at the Apex Records skyscraper to allocate the ten global streaming spots.","The moment he stepped into the ground-floor lobby, he realized Director Vance had leaked the news of the auction to the entire talent roster.","The lobby was packed with every artist signed to the Apex conglomerate.","\"Mr. Lawson!\" an actress pleaded, pushing her way to the front of the mob. \"My international demographics perfectly align with the Global Soundwave network! Please, I just need one spot!\"","\"Boss, I will do anything for a placement!\" a pop star yelled, throwing herself at Jude’s chest.","With his newly acquired skills active, Jude scanned the crowd.","He could instantly see the artificiality in their desperate smiles, the curated personas designed to manipulate his favor.","He found the desperation annoying... He wasn’t interested in being surrounded by flatterers.","Jude’s gaze swept over the mob and landed on two girls standing on the periphery of the lobby.","Lyla and Mia hadn’t joined the surge. They were simply watching him with genuine respect.","\"Lyla. Mia,\" Jude’s voice carried across the floor.","The two girls blinked, pointing to themselves in shock.","\"You two will take the first two global headliner spots,\" Jude announced firmly.","The rest of the talent roster gasped, their eyes darting toward the two pop stars.","\"As for the remaining eight spots,\" Jude continued, his gaze sweeping over the crowd of celebrities. \"Apex Media and The Sirens will divide them. I am not interested in your desperate pitches. You will earn those remaining spots through performance metrics and loyalty to this conglomerate. Whoever proves themselves to be the most valuable asset will get the placement. Are we clear?\"","\"Yes, Mr. Lawson!\" the crowd responded.","Lyla and Mia’s faces lit up with excitement.","Without waiting for the mob of celebrities to recover, Jude walked out of the doors, leaving the entertainment industry behind him."]},{"number":34,"title":"Chapter 34: Conflict of Interest","paragraphs":["Federal Bureau of Investigation, Financial Crimes Division.","A young federal agent stormed into the bullpen, clutching a stack of financial dossiers.","He threw the files down onto his desk, the crack causing everyone in the office to look up from their monitors.","\"We have been investigating Jude Lawson for a month since the Zenith Motors takeover, and this is everything we have?\" the young agent cursed.","\"The man is a ghost,\" one of the forensic accountants sighed, rubbing his temples. \"He rarely leaves a digital trail. The data in those files is the result of us working day and night, tracing routing numbers through Switzerland, the Cayman Islands, and Luxembourg. And every single wire transfer clears international banking regulations perfectly.\"","\"Perfectly?\" the young agent scoffed. \"If a twenty-something kid suddenly drops billions of dollars in liquid cash to execute hostile takeovers of major conglomerates, there has to be a trace of illicit origin somewhere! You don’t just generate billions out of thin air!\"","\"But look at what we’ve actually found!\" the accountant shot back. \"The most serious infractions are aggressive corporate coercion, minor SEC reporting delays, and a few assault charges leveled against some underground fixers who won’t even testify against him!\"","The young agent grew agitated, slamming his hand flat against the desk. \"I refuse to believe Jude Lawson hasn’t gotten his hands dirty with international wire fraud or racketeering in all this time!\"","A hand landed on his shoulder, making him jump.","The young agent turned. \"Supervisory Agent Thorne.\"","The other analysts in the bullpen also rose to their feet. \"Agent Thorne.\"","Saul Thorne, a veteran investigator, gave a nod before looking at the young agent. \"Shouting about it in the bullpen won’t do a damn bit of good. We build federal RICO cases based on hard evidence, and a federal judge signs warrants based on that evidence. We don’t prosecute based on rumors from rival CEOs.\"","\"But Agent Thorne,\" the young investigator pleaded, gesturing at the files. \"With the evidence we have against Lawson right now, he’ll get a minor corporate fine at most. Everyone in the financial sector knows who he is and the leverage he possesses. I can’t believe he doesn’t have a single count of money laundering to his name.\"","Saul Thorne’s reply was calm. \"Evidence. Let the financial ledgers do the talking.\"","\"Agent Thorne, we’ve investigated almost every corporate entity connected to Lawson,\" the forensic accountant interjected, opening a file. \"His inner circle is tight. All the subsidiaries in his name are clean... if there was dirty money, he’s laundered it so thoroughly that the IRS can’t even find a misplaced decimal point.\"","\"Based on the infractions we can prove against Lawson, a federal judge won’t even authorize a subpoena, let alone the confiscation of his corporate empire,\" the young agent muttered bitterly.","These words plunged the Financial Crimes bullpen into silence.","Just then, there was a knock on the door of the bullpen.","\"Agent Thorne,\" a junior agent called out. \"Agent Shepherd’s team just returned from serving a routine inquiry at Apex Studios, that new joint venture Lawson acquired. They brought back someone with close ties to him. Do you want to handle the questioning personally?\"","Saul Thorne nodded firmly. \"I’ll go. Set up Interview Room Four.\"","Inside the interview room, Harper sat in a chair.","She was wearing her vintage denim jacket, looking out of place in the sterile federal building.","A female agent poured her a glass of water from a pitcher.","\"No need to be nervous, Ms. Harper,\" the female agent said. \"This is just a standard interview room, not a hostile interrogation. Just answer truthfully to whatever we ask you in a bit.\"","Harper didn’t look nervous in the slightest. She smiled and nodded, her hands resting on the table.","Soon, footsteps approached from the hallway outside. Agent Shepherd, who had been leaning against the doorframe, straightened up.","The opened, and Saul Thorne walked in, holding a legal notepad.","Their eyes met.","For a moment, Saul Thorne froze in the doorway.","He stared at Harper, his brain convinced he must be hallucinating.","The President of Apex Studios, the billionaire’s newest corporate lieutenant... was his girlfriend?","Harper looked up at him as well. Her expression was simple, almost blank, as if she had expected this exact scene to unfold eventually given his line of work.","\"Agent Thorne?\" Agent Shepherd called out.","Saul Thorne composed himself, his jaw clenching tightly.","He turned to Agent Shepherd. \"I’m recusing myself from this interview.\"","Agent Shepherd nodded.","Saul Thorne gave Harper one long look. He turned on his heel and left the interview room without saying another word.","Agent Shepherd looked at Harper, surprised to find her calm, showing no emotional reaction to her boyfriend’s sudden departure.","Agent Shepherd opened his notepad and began the interview. \"No need to be nervous. Just answer our questions regarding your employer, and you can leave when we’re done.\"","Harper nodded.","Agent Shepherd clicked his pen. \"When did you first meet Jude Lawson?\"","\"Recently,\" Harper answered smoothly.","Agent Shepherd frowned slightly. \"So you’ve only known him for a very short period of time?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"You’ve known a billionaire for just a few days, and you are already the President of his multi-billion-dollar film studio? It seems you two have a very unique relationship.\"","\"Yes, we do.\"","Agent Shepherd leaned forward, resting his elbows on the table. \"Are you just business partners who work well together, or is there another kind of relationship privately? Are you romantically involved with the target?\"","\"No,\" Harper smiled faintly. \"He’s my mentor. You could say he’s like a sworn brother to me. He protects my creative vision.\"","Agent Shepherd narrowed his eyes. \"Brother? To your recollection, has Mr. Lawson ever mentioned his past to you? The source of his capital?\"","\"No.\"","\"Not even once? For instance, his struggles coming up in the financial world, the identity of his offshore backers, or any corporate enemies he’s made in the shadows? Nothing?\"","\"No,\" Harper replied, unbothered. \"When we’re together, we discuss our film projects and the studio’s creative direction. I know nothing about his financial past.\"","Harper’s gaze never wavered once.","Her eyes were clear and bright, and her answers came without a single moment’s hesitation, showing no sign of careful deliberation or panic.","The reason Harper was calm was because Jude Lawson had sat her down in the executive lobby just yesterday and given her one guarantee.","\"I will never ask you to lie for me, Harper,\" Jude had told her. \"Anything I tell you is something you can freely repeat to the authorities. Anything you’re not supposed to say, I will simply never tell you in the first place.\"","Because of this promise, Harper knew she didn’t need to lie, and that nothing she said in this room could ever threaten or harm the empire of the man who had changed her life..."]},{"number":35,"title":"Chapter 35: Backing Lexi","paragraphs":["While the federal authorities spun their wheels in utter frustration, Jude was sitting in the back of his Maybach, gliding through the city’s financial district.","He had spent the early morning finalizing the integration of Apex Records and Zenith Motors, but his mind had now shifted back to the digital inventory screen hovering in his vision.","During the Global Soundwave auction, the Platinum Box had awarded him three one-hundred-million-dollar slush funds.","The *Luxury Real Estate* and *Bespoke Assets* funds were straightforward.","The *Digital Media* slush fund stated it could only be routed through live broadcasting platforms, digital content donations, and social media ecosystems.","He needed an avenue to burn through the capital.","Jude pulled out his smartphone and opened his encrypted messaging app, navigating to a contact he hadn’t spoken to since his first week with the system.","Lexi.","She was a high-tier live-streamer who had tried to use Jude for clout.","Jude had humbled her, demonstrating a level of wealth that had left her fiercely loyal.","Jude typed a quick message: *Are there any major broadcast events happening on your network today?*","Ten seconds later, the typing bubble appeared.","Lexi: *Yes! There’s a massive outdoor brand activation and a digital leaderboard tournament today. Do you want me to secure a VIP pass for you?*","Jude: *Is the event highly populated? I need an excuse to clear some digital capital.*","Lexi sent a playful emoji. *Tons of gorgeous streamers will be there. Tell me your type, and I’ll introduce you to the best on the platform.*","Jude chuckled at her pandering. She was an opportunist, but he appreciated the transactional honesty.","Jude: *I’ll pick you up at your agency in twenty minutes. Ensure you are streaming. I am going to back you today.*","Lexi’s reply was a string of excited exclamation points.","Thirty minutes later, the Maybach pulled up to the curb outside of the city’s largest influencer agency.","Lexi was standing on the sidewalk, holding her stabilizing gimbal and streaming to her live chat.","Standing next to her was a younger girl wearing designer streetwear, looking nervously at the massive vehicle.","As Jude stepped out of the Maybach, Lexi beamed.","She hurried over, angling her camera away from Jude’s face to respect his privacy.","\"Mr. Lawson!\" Lexi greeted him. \"Thank you so much for coming. I want you to meet Sienna. She’s a new streamer at my agency, and she’s partnering with me for the outdoor event today.\"","Sienna stepped forward, her eyes wide.","\"Wow,\" Sienna said, looking at Jude with awe. \"Lexi told me her primary backer was a titan, but this is insane. It is an honor to meet you, Boss. Thank you for sponsoring our broadcast today!\"","Sienna’s flattery was so saccharine it bordered on theatrical, but Jude found it refreshing compared to the corporate speak of the Wall Street executives he usually dealt with.","\"Nice to meet you, Sienna,\" Jude said smoothly. \"Get in.\"","Sienna slid into the interior of the Maybach.","As the driver pulled away from the curb, Lexi leaned forward.","\"The event is being hosted at the newly constructed underground luxury promenade,\" Lexi explained, checking her chat feed. \"A dozen high-end designer brands are sponsoring a digital leaderboard. Every major streamer in the city is going to be broadcasting simultaneously from the promenade. The streamer who generates the highest volume of digital donations during the two-hour window wins the grand prize... a massive corporate sponsorship payout.\"","\"And you want the payout?\" Jude asked.","\"We don’t care about the brand payout,\" Sienna chimed in, shaking her head. \"We just want the agency bonus! Our streaming network gives a fifty-thousand-dollar cash bonus to whichever of their streamers takes first place on the overall leaderboard.\"","Lexi nodded eagerly. \"Exactly! The clout of placing first on the regional leaderboard is worth ten times the brand payout for our channel metrics.\"","Jude smiled. If they wanted first place, they were going to get it...","[Ding!]","[Continuous Mission Triggered: Digital Supremacy.]","[Objective: The digital landscape is simply another arena for capital dominance. Secure the absolute first-place ranking on the live broadcast leaderboard and humiliate the opposition.]","[Reward: +1 Money Sign-In, +1 Platinum System Reward Box!]","The mission didn’t even require effort. Jude had a hundred-million-dollar slush fund literally burning a hole in his system inventory.","It wasn’t a matter of if he would win, but by how many millions he would shatter the existing platform records...","Ten minutes later, the Maybach descended into the VIP parking garage of the luxury promenade.","The moment Jude, Lexi, and Sienna stepped out of the private elevator banks and onto the main promenade, it was obvious the event was already in full swing.","The walkway was swarming with dozens of streamers holding selfie sticks and ring lights.","However, two crowds had formed near the center of the promenade, dominating the foot traffic.","At the epicenter stood two of the most famous influencers on the continent.","One was \"Titan,\" a loud hype-streamer whose channel boasted over five million active subscribers.","The other was \"Vixen,\" a beauty guru whose audience was equally massive.","Titan was currently holding his camera high above his head, shouting into the microphone while his fans screamed in the background.","\"Listen up, chat!\" Titan roared, flexing his arms. \"You already know how this leaderboard is going to end! I’ve teamed up with the Queen herself, Vixen! Our channels are linked for the donation drive!\"","Titan turned and pointed mockingly at the dozens of smaller streamers hovering on the periphery of the crowd.","\"To all the other streamers in the building, I suggest you just pack up your ring lights and go home!\" Titan boasted. \"Vixen and I are taking first and second place on the leaderboard today. It’s a mathematical certainty! You can all fight over the scraps for third place!\"","The smaller streamers exchanged looks. It was demoralizing...","Titan and Vixen had millions of fans.","Competing against their combined digital ecosystem was impossible for a mid-tier streamer.","Vixen flipped her hair, barely glancing at the crowd. \"Don’t even try to snipe the top spot, guys. Our whales are locked and loaded. The leaderboard is closed.\"","Lexi gritted her teeth, her grip tightening on her gimbal. \"They are so arrogant. Titan always pulls this stunt.\"","Sienna, however, was not intimidated...","She had just ridden in a Maybach with a billionaire.","Sienna stepped forward, cupping her hands around her mouth.","\"You guys can have third place!\" Sienna yelled back across the floor. \"Because our Patron is taking first place for us today!\"","Titan paused his broadcast, lowering his camera.","He turned his head, his eyes narrowing as he locked onto Sienna.","Vixen stopped touching up her makeup, glaring at the new girl."]},{"number":36,"title":"Chapter 36: Walking Away Clean","paragraphs":["Meanwhile, across the city at the Federal Bureau of Investigation, Harper answered every question honestly and conscientiously...","She didn’t hide what she knew regarding the creative operations at Apex Studios, nor did she say a word more than necessary about what she didn’t.","Her demeanor made it abundantly clear to Agent Shepherd that she wasn’t lying.","Supervisory Agent Saul Thorne leaned against the cinderblock wall of the federal corridor, his gaze fixed on the door of Interview Room Four.","His career in the Financial Crimes division required clinical detachment. But today, an uncontrollable tightness constricted his chest, and his mind was a mess.","Harper had never mentioned Jude Lawson in front of him. Not a single word.","He had never imagined that Harper, an indie filmmaker who preferred vintage thrift stores to corporate boardrooms, would have any connection to a corporate raider like Lawson.","Time ticked by... The initial shock slowly gave way to fear.","He was afraid that Jude Lawson’s shadow-laced financial empire would truly implicate Harper.","He was even more afraid that she would cover for Lawson and become a federal accomplice!","About forty minutes later, the door of Interview Room Four finally opened.","Agent Shepherd was the first to emerge. He looked up, adjusting his tie, and saw Saul Thorne waiting by the door. He walked over and spoke in a low voice.","\"Agent Thorne, we’ve asked everything we needed to regarding her appointment,\" Agent Shepherd said. \"We didn’t find anything suspicious. Your girlfriend and Jude Lawson appear to have a protective brother-sister dynamic, but she genuinely doesn’t know much about his offshore financial affairs.\"","Saul Thorne’s pupils constricted. Brother and sister... this was obviously not just ordinary corporate employment!","\"You had no idea she was the President of his studio?\" Agent Shepherd asked, reading Saul’s expression.","Saul Thorne shook his head, a hollow feeling settling in his stomach.","Agent Shepherd sighed.","He reached out, patted Saul’s shoulder, and tried to comfort him. \"You need to try and relax about this, Saul. The division will be investigating your girlfriend’s corporate footprint closely. If she isn’t found to be harboring his illicit funds, you don’t need to take this so seriously.\"","Soon, Harper also came out of the room, escorted by the female agent. Her expression was serene.","Agent Shepherd knew Saul Thorne would have things to say to his girlfriend, so he gave them space, beckoning the female agent to leave the corridor with him.","Saul Thorne looked at Harper, struggling to find his voice, but ultimately, he didn’t know what to say.","Harper smiled faintly. \"Walk me out first.\"","They walked out of the federal building side by side. Saul Thorne didn’t reach out to take her hand, but Harper felt no sense of loss at the distance between them.","She knew Saul Thorne, and she understood the nature of his badge.","Saul Thorne didn’t stop walking until they were out the main entrance, standing on the steps under the overcast city sky. He looked at Harper, his expression complex, and finally spoke.","\"Why didn’t you tell me?\" Saul demanded.","Harper tilted her head up slightly to look at him.","To this day, she had never tired of looking at Saul Thorne’s face...","It was still just as handsome and sharply defined as when they had first met.","But at this precise moment, she was more clear-headed than she had ever been in her entire life.","\"I’m not a suspect, Saul, much less a criminal. I have no obligation to come clean to you about my employment or my corporate benefactors,\" Harper said, her tone remarkably calm. \"Besides, my relationship with him is my own personal affair. It has nothing to do with anyone else in this building, and I’m not obligated to tell anyone about it.\"","A flash of pain crossed Saul Thorne’s eyes, his voice rising in desperation. \"But he’s not a good person, Harper! He is a ruthless corporate raider! You’re so close to him, you had to have known he destroys companies and ruins lives!\"","\"I understand what you mean.\" Harper nodded, her tone shifted, hardening slightly. \"But everyone in this world has their own unique perspective from which they view people and things.\"","Saul stared at her, bewildered.","\"From your point of view at the Bureau, of course he’s a bad man,\" Harper continued. \"From the point of view of Wall Street, and maybe even most of the corporate world, he’s a monster. But to the artists he protects... to the people he elevates from nothing... and from my point of view... he’s a good brother and an incredible mentor.\"","Saul Thorne’s expression twisted into agony.","And Harper knew of Saul Thorne’s dedication to his identity as a federal agent.","So she gave a smile and said, \"Saul, I’ve been very happy during my time with you. But now, we both know it’s over.\"","From the very beginning, all she had wanted was a simple romance...","But now, Jude Lawson was like a thorn that would forever be stuck in Saul Thorne’s heart.","Once a rift of this magnitude formed between them, the relationship would no longer be pure but would instead become complicated by federal subpoenas and mutual suspicion.","Harper would never let herself get trapped in such a compromised relationship. She had to get out now.","Because she would not sever ties with Jude Lawson for Saul Thorne. Even if the federal government managed to freeze Jude’s assets or put him on trial, she still had to manage Apex Studios for him.","Furthermore, the classified documents regarding the studio’s creative equity division and several of Jude’s private assets were resting in her safe.","This was Jude Lawson’s trust in her, and she would not betray it.","Saul Thorne looked at Harper, the words to ask her to stay caught in his throat.","If she said it was over, then it was over.","After a long silence, Harper knew Saul Thorne had accepted the end of their relationship. She looked at him, her smile still warm.","\"I know you and your division will continue to investigate me and the studio. You’re a good federal agent; it’s your duty,\" Harper said softly. \"Be it me, or Jude... if that day ever comes where you have to cross that line... I won’t blame you.\"","\"Harper...\" Saul Thorne murmured.","Harper just shook her head.","\"Goodbye, Saul Thorne.\"","Harper turned and walked away down the steps without looking back.","Saul Thorne stood rooted to the spot, watching her figure recede into the distance until she disappeared around the corner.","Bound by his badge and his pride, he still didn’t say the words to make her stay...","Meanwhile, Harper got into her vintage car parked at the curb.","Sitting in the driver’s seat, she let out a sigh.","The sudden end of the relationship didn’t seem to have a devastating impact on her; she just felt deep down that it was a genuine shame.","But as she pulled away from the curb, heading back toward the monolith of Apex Media, her mind was at peace. Her loyalty belonged to Jude Lawson."]},{"number":37,"title":"Chapter 37: A Visit to the Backlot","paragraphs":["Her phone suddenly vibrated against the passenger seat.","The encrypted caller ID simply read: *Boss.*","Harper collected her thoughts, took a deep breath, and answered the call through the car’s Bluetooth system.","\"Jude?\"","Jude Lawson paused for a fraction of a second before speaking, his voice calm. \"Are you out of the federal building?\"","\"I just got out.\" Harper forced a laugh and asked, \"Did Director Vance panic and tell you?\"","\"Did the agents give you a hard time?\" Jude ignored her question.","\"No, I just answered whatever they asked.\" As Harper spoke. \"Jude, I finally understand why you gave me that speech in the lobby yesterday. When I was sitting in that interrogation room, I was calm. My conscience was clear. I didn’t have to worry that my words might trigger a perjury charge, and I didn’t have to consider whether I should lie to cover for your offshore accounts.\"","\"Lying to a federal agent and committing perjury carry severe prison sentences,\" Jude replied. \"You run my studio, Harper, so I have an obligation to protect you. I will not let you get legally implicated in my broader acquisitions.\"","\"Besides,\" Jude added. \"I’ve already entrusted you with the majority of Apex Media’s creative equity. There’s a selfish reason for me to protect your public record, so don’t overthink the sentimentality. If the FBI ever does manage to find traction on me, you’ll be the one keeping the studio alive.\"","\"That’s all for now,\" Jude said. \"Maya will contact you this afternoon regarding the transfer of our new global broadcasting assets. Harper... take care of yourself.\"","After hanging up the call, Harper sat in the idling car.","Without a hesitation, she took out her phone, opened her contacts, and deleted all information related to Saul Thorne.","...","Apex Studios Headquarters.","Several weeks later, Isabella Frost... one of the studio’s fastest-rising young actresses knocked lightly on the door of Connie’s office.","\"Well, look who it is! Isabella?\"","Connie, a veteran talent manager, was surprised to see her star client.","She put down her tablet and stood up to greet her warmly. \"You’ve been quiet for the last month in your acting workshops. What brings you to the executive floor all of a sudden?\"","Isabella smiled, returning the greeting before explaining her reason for coming. \"Connie, I’ve finished reading that script you sent me last week, and I’ve made my final decision.\"","Connie’s eyes lit up at her words. \"You’re willing to take it?\"","Isabella nodded.","\"That’s more like it! I told you you’d be deeply interested in the character once you actually read the script. It’ll be a whole new creative challenge for you.\"","\"The character is what drew me in,\" Isabella admitted, sitting down in the chair. \"I want to give it a try, but I just don’t know if I can do her justice on screen.\"","Connie happily took Isabella’s hands to encourage her. \"No problem at all! Plus, this is a serious prestige drama. Mr. Lawson has authorized a massive budget for it, so most of the main and supporting cast are veteran A-listers with superb skills. If you can get on this production, you’re guaranteed to learn a lot.\"","\"Did Heather Keaton take the part?\" Isabella asked hopefully.","\"Of course she did. How could a veteran turn down such a phenomenal script?\" Connie said with a wide smile. \"This way, she’ll be the female lead, and you’ll be the second female lead. Since you’re both my clients under the Apex umbrella, she can look out for you on set.\"","Hearing this, Isabella’s lips curved into a delighted smile.","\"So if you’re sure you’re taking it, I’ll confirm the casting with the production team right now!\" Connie said, reaching for her phone.","\"Okay. By the way, Connie, I heard the *Crimson Dynasty* crew is filming on the Apex backlot recently. I want to go visit Yuna and Finn.\"","While Isabella had been on a month-long break for her immersive acting workshops, the company had assigned her two personal assistants, Yuna and Finn, to other artists to keep them on the payroll.","Connie nodded. \"No problem. I think they’re currently assigned to Rachel Farris’s team right now. Do you need me to give her manager a heads-up?\"","\"That would be great. It would be a little rude to just show up to her set unannounced.\"","Connie smiled. \"I’ll let them know now. I’ll print you a VIP pass for the backlot in a bit, and you can take a golf cart straight there.\"","After leaving the executive tower, Isabella grabbed an iced coffee and headed directly out to the studio backlot.","On the way, she sent a quick text message to Yuna ahead of time, but she never got a reply.","Getting through the security checkpoints was easy with the VIP pass.","Isabella quickly navigated the maze of soundstages and found the outdoor set for *Crimson Dynasty*.","\"Ms. Frost?\"","She ran into a production assistant at the entrance to the set. \"What are you doing all the way out here? Are you slated for a cameo?\"","Isabella denied it, smiling politely. \"No, no, I’m just here to visit the set.\"","She tapped her VIP pass against the lanyard on her chest as she spoke.","\"Oh, who are you here to see? They’re filming an exterior shot inside. Let me take you in!\"","\"I’m here to see Yuna and Finn. They’re my personal assistants,\" Isabella explained. \"I’ve been on a workshop break, so the company assigned them to Ms. Farris’s team to keep their hours up.\"","\"Oh...\" The man nodded in understanding. \"I think I just saw Ms. Farris over at Exterior Stage 1. Let me take you inside first.\"","\"Thank you!\"","It was a Victorian-era drama, and the background actors on set were all wearing period costumes.","When they reached a spot behind the camera tracks, the man pointed to a canopy not far away and whispered, \"Ms. Frost, Ms. Farris is over there. See? Is that your assistant, Yuna, next to her?\"","Isabella followed his finger and looked over.","She saw Rachel Farris, dressed in modern casual clothes, reclining lazily on a rocking chair underneath the shade of a production tent.","Yuna, however, was not under the tent.","Yuna was standing out in the direct sunlight, holding a UV umbrella over Rachel with one hand and a fan with the other, half-squatting just to shield the older actress from the glare.","The outdoor temperature had reached ninety-five degrees, yet Yuna herself was exposed to the sun.","Sweat poured down her face, and her skin was much darker than the last time Isabella had seen her.","Not only that, but a backpack was slung over Yuna’s shoulder...","Yuna’s body was shaking, looking ready to collapse at any moment.","Meanwhile, other actors were also resting on the sidelines between takes, but they had all found shady spots to sit.","Even those accompanied by assistants were, at most, just being handed water bottles or scripts when they needed them.","Isabella’s heart sank, and a surge of anger washed over her."]},{"number":38,"title":"Chapter 38: Ungrateful","paragraphs":["Yuna’s conspicuous predicament made it clear to the production assistant that the actress was making things as difficult as possible for the young girl.","Rachel Farris was a respected veteran actress within the industry.","While there were occasional rumors about her being \"high-maintenance\" on set, no one had ever publicly accused her of being harsh with her team.","Because Rachel’s on-screen roles were of the wholesome variety, people who didn’t know her would assume she was easygoing in her private life.","Just then, Yuna, exhausted by the heat, swayed on her feet.","The momentary lapse in the umbrella’s shadow earned her a glare from Rachel, whose eyes were filled with harshness.","\"Ms. Frost, this current scene is almost finished,\" the production assistant whispered, touching Isabella’s arm. \"Could you wait a little while before approaching? The director is running a master shot right now.\"","No matter what her rising status was at Apex Studios, Isabella was still a junior compared to a veteran like Rachel Farris.","Although Isabella was angry, she understood set etiquette. She didn’t want to ruin a take for the crew, so she just nodded and waited off to the side of the camera tracks.","When the director called \"Cut!\" and the scene wrapped, the crowd grew noisy. Isabella walked toward Rachel Farris’s tent.","\"Rachel, your next scene isn’t until this evening,\" Yuna’s weak voice drifted over as Isabella approached. \"Why don’t you go rest in your air-conditioned car for a bit?\"","Yuna really couldn’t hold on any longer.","Unexpectedly, Rachel didn’t bother to glance up, \"My doctor said I have too much dampness in my body and my joints have been aching. He told me to get more natural sun.\"","Yuna lowered her head.","She was angry and didn’t dare show it to the actress, only saying with grievance, \"Rachel, I really can’t hold on much longer. I think I’m going to pass out. How about I go get Linda to take care of you for a while?\"","\"Linda? She’s a clumsy newcomer who just joined the management company. What would she possibly know about being a personal assistant?\" Rachel shot Yuna a sharp glance, her tone unkind. \"I let you follow me because I think highly of you. Do you think just anyone gets an opportunity like this? Don’t be ungrateful for the blessings you have.\"","Yuna was speechless.","Anyone with eyes could see she was being tormented for no logical reason.","Yuna knew why she was being targeted.","Rachel had wanted a different script that had gone to another Apex actress, and she was taking her frustration out on the closest subordinate.","Just then, a familiar voice called her name across the asphalt.","\"Yuna!\"","Her legs gave out, and she collapsed onto the ground.","The sun umbrella and the fan in her hands fell to the side.","Startled by the sudden noise and the loss of her shade, Rachel shot up from her rocking chair in annoyance. \"What is wrong with you, you clumsy idiot?!\"","The commotion drew the glances of other actors and crew members.","However, seeing it was just Rachel making things difficult for her assistant again, they went back to their own business, unwilling to get involved with the diva.","\"S-Sorry, I lost my footing.\"","Yuna apologized from the ground. Isabella rushed to her side in a couple of quick strides, reaching out to help her up. \"Yuna, are you okay? You’re burning up.\"","\"Isabella?\"","Yuna stared in surprise at Isabella Frost’s pretty face.","The next second, her eyes reddened as she asked, her voice choking up with emotion, \"W-What are you doing here?\"","\"I came to get you and Finn,\" Isabella said, pulling the backpack off Yuna’s shoulder and setting it aside.","Originally, she had just wanted to visit them on the backlot...","But after witnessing everything that had happened, Isabella had made up her mind.","She was taking them with her today.","\"Who are you?\"","Rachel Farris stared at the young woman for a moment before demanding an answer.","Isabella helped Yuna to her feet, steadying the trembling girl, before turning to face Rachel. \"Hello, Ms. Farris. My name is Isabella Frost.\"","\"Isabella Frost?\" Rachel’s gaze swept over Isabella doubtfully from head to toe before a look of realization dawned on her face. \"Oh, right, I remember now. I’ve heard people at the management company mention you.\"","As she spoke, her lips curled into a smile as she looked past Isabella to the red-eyed Yuna.","\"Yuna was your personal assistant before, wasn’t she? And that Finn guy?\"","Isabella nodded, keeping her posture straight, \"I’m about to start a new prestige project for the studio, so I came to take them back today. If you’re currently short-staffed, Ms. Farris, you can request more people from the company.\"","\"Huh?\" Rachel’s mouth fell open in surprise.","She looked around the set before turning back to Isabella. \"Do you have any idea how things work in this industry? The management company assigned these assistants to me for the full duration of this project. If they don’t finish the project, they breach their contracts, and I can’t pay them.\"","\"That’s fine. I’ll pay their salaries,\" Isabella said without missing a beat, then turned to Yuna. \"Hand over everything you have that belongs to Ms. Farris, then go get Finn and come with me.\"","Every single day serving Rachel felt like walking to her own execution.","\"Hold on!\"","Seeing how Isabella was showing her disrespect in front of the crew, Rachel’s expression darkened drastically. \"Little girl, are you actually trying to snatch people right out from under me on my own set?\"","Facing a twenty-something Isabella, Rachel’s presence flared up, frightening Yuna so much that the poor assistant didn’t dare move.","Isabella’s face remained calm, but inwardly she was nervous.","This nervousness didn’t come from fear of Rachel, but from the fact that her current actions were the complete opposite of her usual personality.","\"Ms. Farris, I’m not snatching them from you. I’m simply asking for them back,\" Isabella said, still maintaining a reasonable tone. \"They’ve been with me ever since I joined the company, and I’ve grown very accustomed to having them take care of me.\"","Isabella took a deep breath. \"Back when I was about to take my workshop break, I told Connie that if the company was short-staffed, they could reassign them, but they’d come back to me the moment I was ready to start my next project. Connie agreed to those terms at the time.\"","Rachel’s brows shot up in anger. \"Are you trying to use Connie to pressure me? Do you think dropping a senior manager’s name scares me?\"","\"That’s not my intention at all. I’m just informing you of the situation exactly as it was established,\" Isabella replied.","As she said this, she was already pulling out her phone from her purse.","\"Or perhaps I should give Connie a call right now so you can confirm with her directly?\""]},{"number":39,"title":"Chapter 39: Federal Shame","paragraphs":["Isabella’s bold move made Rachel Farris choke with sudden indignation.","If Connie got involved, Rachel would look like a tyrant bullying a rising star over a scheduling technicality.","Rachel Farris glared down at Yuna, a smile spreading across her face.","She nodded slowly and said, \"Fine. Since her former master has come all the way down here to claim her, I suppose I can’t just keep her against her will. You were never a good fit for a production of this caliber anyway.\"","She deliberately emphasized the word \"master.\"","Yuna looked up at Rachel Farris, bowing her head, and said, \"Thank you, Rachel!\"","Rachel Farris snorted, turned on her heel, and walked away toward the caterers.","\"What’s going on? Why is she treating you like this, Yuna?\"","Isabella took Yuna’s trembling hand, guiding her toward the exit of the soundstage.","At that precise moment, safely away from the crew, all the grievances Yuna had bottled up finally burst forth, and she began to cry openly. \"Just because someone on the makeup team was complaining to me that she’s high-maintenance, I foolishly brought you up and praised you, saying how nice you are and how easy you make our jobs... and she happened to overhear the conversation.\"","\"Just for that?\" Isabella was genuinely shocked.","Yuna nodded, tears streaming down her face. \"Because of that one incident, she requested that the production coordinator assign me to her side.\"","\"Isabella...\" Yuna sobbed, hugging the actress. \"Thank goodness you’re here. Thank you so much for saving me. I don’t know how much longer I could have held on out there.\"","\"Okay, no more crying. Go pack your things, get Finn, and come home to the main studio with me today.\"","Isabella decided not to report the matter to Connie.","If Rachel Farris was bold enough to act this way in front of dozens of crew members, she clearly wasn’t afraid of word getting out to management!","\"Finn, are you okay?\"","On the golf cart ride back to the executive tower, Isabella made sure to check in on Finn, who had just rushed over from the props department with Yuna’s bags.","Finn shook his head. \"I’m fine. I just feel terrible for Yuna. I never thought an actress like Rachel Farris would be so deeply unprofessional behind the scenes.\"","Yuna, however, looked at Isabella with concern. \"Isabella, you went directly against her today for our sake. Someone as petty as her won’t just let this go. I’m worried she’s going to use her industry connections to make things difficult for you now.\"","\"We’ll cross that bridge when we come to it. I couldn’t just stand by and watch you suffer.\"","\"Okay, let’s change the subject.\" Isabella patted Yuna’s hand and smiled brightly. \"I just landed a new role. Filming starts next month. I’m the second female lead in *Neon Shadows*, and I’ll be working directly with Heather Keaton.\"","\"Really?!\"","Isabella nodded. \"From now on, you’ll both always be with me on set. I won’t let the company reassign you to anyone else again.\"","Hearing this, Yuna and Finn exchanged an excited glance and nodded.","***","A week later...","Global Soundwave had spent a fortune to acquire the exclusive online broadcasting rights.","On the day of its premiere, the show dominated the trending topics on all major media outlets and social platforms.","The hashtag for Isabella Frost’s character also quickly went viral after her appearance in the second episode.","Her personal social media account came roaring back to life as she experienced a surge in followers.","Isabella posted several behind-the-scenes photos. Each post surpassed hundreds of thousands of shares and likes.","On the day of the premiere, Harper, as the President of Apex Studios, gathered the executive board and the talent roster at the penthouse corporate suites, making everyone sit down and watch the studio’s debut.","Besides Isabella, Yuna, and Finn, Maya and Director Vance were naturally in attendance...","***","Harper received her first call from Maya three days later.","Harper pressed the answer button on her dashboard console, and the moment Maya said, \"They’re here,\" Harper’s blood ran cold.","When she rushed to the scene twenty minutes later, a dozen black federal SUVs and several marked police cruisers were parked outside the gated corporate estate where Jude Lawson resided.","A crowd of onlookers, reporters, and employees had gathered at the perimeter to watch the commotion.","Just as she pushed her way into the dense crowd near the gates, a hand grabbed her shoulder.","\"Harper!\"","It was Director Vance.","Rainwater trickled down Harper’s hair and onto her pale cheeks.","She looked at Director Vance, and the executive just shook his head at her with a grim expression. \"It’s over. The warrants are signed. All we can do now is watch them take him.\"","Director Vance had barely finished speaking when a stir went through the crowd of reporters.","\"He’s coming out! They’re bringing Lawson out!\"","\"I thought the guy was untouchable. I heard he had billionaires and politicians in his pocket.\"","\"It’s a direct financial crackdown from the federal level this time. He’s not getting away with the Zenith takeover.\"","It was as if the curtain of rain muffled all the noise around her...","In the distance, walking down the grand marble steps of the estate, Jude Lawson was led out by two federal agents, his hands cuffed behind his jacket.","Walking behind him, overseeing the arrest, was Agent Shepherd, the man who had questioned Harper the other day... and Saul Thorne!","Standing near the doors of the estate, Maya watched with her eyes brimming with tears.","Harper’s gaze was fixed entirely on Jude’s face, her eyes never leaving him as he walked through the rain.","As if sensing her stare through the sea of reporters, Jude suddenly looked up, and his eyes met Harper’s in the crowd.","Harper didn’t speak, nor did her lips move, but Jude suddenly smiled at her.","The smile lasted only two seconds before the federal agents pushed him into the back of the armored SUV.","Harper looked away from the vehicle, and when her eyes shifted slightly, they fell directly upon Saul Thorne, who was standing in the freezing rain and had also just spotted her in the crowd.","Their eyes met.","Saul Thorne watched Harper for a long moment, the rain soaking through his windbreaker, before a sad smile finally touched his eyes."]},{"number":40,"title":"Chapter 40: Evidence","paragraphs":["The executive boardroom at Pierce Studios was deathly silent.","Every shareholder and executive had their eyes fixed on the breaking news broadcast playing on the television.","The screen showed footage of Jude Lawson being led into a federal SUV.","\"Well,\" Maxwell Pierce, the elderly Chairman of the studio, said with a slow nod. \"It seems the Wall Street prodigy finally flew too close to the sun. The federal authorities will tie his assets up in litigation for years. Apex Media is bleeding in the water.\"","Sitting near the head of the table, Donovan Pierce fought to hide a smug smile.","\"I told you, Grandfather,\" Donovan said, adjusting his tie. \"Lawson’s entire empire was built on a house of cards. With him out of the picture, we can absorb their market share.\"","Suddenly, the doors of the boardroom burst open with a crash.","The executives jumped in their chairs, turning toward the entrance.","Strolling into the boardroom, his charcoal suit perfectly tailored, was Jude Lawson.","Flanking Jude were two private military contractors. They were dragging a bruised man by the collar of his shirt.","With a casual shove, they threw the man forward, sending him crashing onto the boardroom carpet.","Maxwell Pierce stood up abruptly, his face flushing with anger. \"Lawson! What is the meaning of this?! How the hell are you not in federal custody?!\"","\"The FBI realized very quickly that they didn’t have a single shred of actionable evidence to hold me,\" Jude replied, his tone calm. \"So I decided to spend my afternoon taking out the trash instead.\"","Jude gestured down at the bruised man groaning on the carpet.","\"Who is this person?\" Maxwell demanded, staring at the battered figure.","\"His name is Silas Grey,\" Jude explained smoothly. \"He is an underground fixer. The man who orchestrated the attempted kidnapping of my artist, Lyla, earlier this week.\"","The entire boardroom gasped collectively.","Donovan Pierce’s face drained of all color, turning a sickening shade of white.","\"You see, Chairman,\" Jude continued, his eyes locking onto Donovan. \"I subdued Silas’s kidnappers and let them lead me directly to his warehouse. I didn’t involve the police immediately because I wanted to know exactly whose corporate payroll he was on.\"","Maxwell Pierce looked down at the unmoving fixer. \"This person doesn’t seem to be moving, Lawson. Could he be dead?\"","\"He wants to die right now,\" Jude said. \"But dying isn’t that easy.\"","Jude walked over and kicked Silas’s ribs with the toe of his shoe. \"Stop playing dead, Silas. Get up and tell the board of directors exactly who ordered you to kidnap my artist.\"","Silas said, his voice weak and trembling, \"It was... Donovan Pierce... who ordered me.\"","\"State his full name and title for the record!\" Jude commanded sharply.","\"Donovan Pierce!\" Silas gasped out. \"The heir to the studio.\"","\"What?!\"","The entire Pierce Studios executive board was shocked.","Maxwell Pierce slammed his hand on the table. \"What are you saying?! Don’t talk absolute nonsense! How could it possibly be Donovan?!\"","The boardroom erupted into heated whispers.","\"It must be a fabrication!\"","Donovan put on an angry facade.","\"This scoundrel is blatantly slandering me! I am innocent!\" Donovan shouted, pointing a finger at Silas. \"Grandfather, you must believe me! How could I do such a barbaric thing?! I don’t even know this person! You can’t believe a single word this underground criminal says!\"","At that moment, a man sitting to the right of the Chairman stood up. \"Lawson, your little espionage story is pretty well-constructed, but how long are you planning to direct and act this out yourself?\"","Jude slowly turned his gaze. The man speaking was Richard Pierce, Donovan’s father and a senior vice president of the studio.","\"And what exactly do you mean by that, Richard?\" Jude asked.","Richard sneered. \"I’m saying the theatrical act put on by you and your security team is quite a show. Where did you find this bruised actor? The makeup is not bad! There was no real kidnapping at all. Everything you just said is fabricated, aiming to frame my son and destabilize our board! Am I wrong?\"","Maxwell Pierce looked at Jude, his eyes narrowing with suspicion. \"Lawson, explain this absurd situation immediately.\"","\"I don’t need to explain reality to you,\" Jude replied. \"The kidnapping attempt is true. The police reports from the street outside Apex Records confirm it.\"","Richard Pierce chuckled, shaking his head. \"Oh, you’re right, Lawson! The police reports also noted that an entire warehouse full of armed underground thugs was dismantled by *one man* before the police arrived! Everyone, listen to this! Could such a person actually exist in the real world? Does that sound believable for a Wall Street billionaire?! Is he some kind of martial arts superhero? It is obviously a fake police report bought with your offshore money!\"","The Pierce family executives, upon hearing this breakdown, felt that Richard made sense.","\"Lawson, you are so vicious! Why are you trying to frame me?! Grandfather, you must stand up for me! He’s trying to harm the Pierce legacy!\" Donovan shouted.","Maxwell Pierce was so angry that his hands were shaking.","He glared at Jude from the head of the table. \"Lawson, your little stunt has failed. How could you possibly be so powerful as to take down an entire underground gang alone? Unless you show me undeniable evidence right now, I will have security throw you out, and I will press charges for corporate slander!\"","Without a single word of defense, Jude calmly reached into his jacket pocket and pulled out a burner phone that he had taken from Silas Grey’s pocket back at the warehouse.","He tapped the screen, turned the volume to maximum, and placed it flat on the table.","A recorded audio conversation echoed crystal clear throughout the boardroom.","\"How does Young Master Pierce want me to entertain her?\" Silas’s voice played from the speaker.","\"That little bitch has already signed a renewal contract with Apex,\"* Donovan’s arrogant voice replied on the recording. \"Once she returns to the studio, she’ll become their golden child. Silas, you help me stage a scandal and force her to resign voluntarily! Ruin her brand completely!\"","\"Damn it, Pierce, that’s too troublesome. The base fee won’t do, gotta add another hundred thousand for the media leak...\"","Upon hearing the recording, every single executive in the Pierce Studios boardroom was paralyzed with shock.","Jude tapped the screen, pausing the recording.","He laughed softly, \"Donovan, do you recognize your own voice? This is you ordering the destruction of a rival asset, isn’t it?\"","Donovan Pierce’s face changed dramatically, his eyes wide.","Silas Grey then lifted his bruised head from the carpet, coughed up a speck of blood, and chuckled. \"Every time I deal with a billionaire, I record the call. I keep a back road for myself as insurance. I didn’t expect it to be useful so soon.\"","\"You might still try to deny it, Richard,\" Jude said, looking at Donovan’s father. \"But that’s perfectly fine. We can have it verified by federal authorities. Moreover, this exact burner phone contains the digital call logs connecting directly to Donovan’s private corporate line! You cannot deny it.\""]},{"number":41,"title":"Chapter 41: Lack of Morality","paragraphs":["The recording released by Jude Lawson included an explicit conversation between the underground fixer, Silas Grey, and Donovan Pierce!","They were discussing the kidnapping of Apex Media’s lead artist!","This recording was real, so Jude wasn’t afraid of the opposing executives questioning its validity.","Moreover, Silas Grey’s call records had several incoming calls directly from Donovan’s private office line.","Everyone in the Pierce boardroom fell into silence..","\"Donovan, you are a despicable scoundrel,\" Jude said. \"You actually used such pathetic means against an innocent artist simply because you couldn’t compete in the open market.\"","Maxwell Pierce was both shocked and furious.","He slammed his hand on the table and glared at Donovan, \"You absolute bastard! How could you do such a stupid thing?!\"","Jude smiled faintly. \"Chairman, don’t be angry just yet. The recording isn’t finished; what’s next is even more exciting!\"","Donovan screamed hoarsely, \"Lawson, stop playing the recording! Yes, it’s me! I admit it! Is that enough for you now?!\"","Jude looked down at him with disdain. \"The content that follows is far too exciting not to share with your board.\"","Saying this, Jude pressed the play button on the burner phone once again.","\"Instead of adding money to the base fee, I have a better idea,\" Donovan’s voice echoed through the boardroom. \"Silas, do you really think Lyla is worth an extra hundred thousand for a simple media leak? Just strip her down and take the photos yourself. I don’t care how rough your men are with her, as long as her pristine brand is destroyed.\"","\"Young Master Pierce, you really are an absolute scoundrel,\" Silas’s recorded voice chuckled darkly. \"Isn’t Lyla universally beloved by the public? You could even think of such a vicious idea for a young girl. I admire your total lack of morality!\"","\"What public? Anyone who stands against the Pierce legacy is my enemy. I wish she were dead. I wonder if you have any personal interest in her, Silas?\"","\"...\"","In this recorded conversation, simply to save a hundred thousand dollars on his extortion budget, Donovan Pierce suggested that Silas Grey harm Lyla!","Hearing these callous words, every executive in the Pierce family boardroom was struck with shock and disgust.","Jude’s eyes narrowed.","\"You bastard! You absolute bastard, kneel before me!\" Maxwell Pierce exploded in rage, slamming his hand on the table so hard that his whiskey glass fell to the floor and shattered into pieces.","Donovan dropped to his knees on the carpet. \"Grandfather, I know I was wrong! It was just a moment of madness fueled by jealousy of Lawson’s new studio! In my fury, I did something foolish. I truly didn’t mean for it to go that far. Please forgive me this once, I’m begging you!\"","Maxwell Pierce shouted in rage. \"A moment of fury?! But you’ve already done it! You almost harmed an innocent girl, and you nearly destroyed the entire Pierce Studios legacy in the process!\"","Jude stepped forward. \"Chairman Pierce, Donovan targeted my lead asset. If not for my personal intervention, Lyla would have fallen victim to his scheme. You must stand up as the leader of this conglomerate and severely punish Donovan! I want him to pay for his actions!\"","Maxwell Pierce grimaced. \"Donovan’s actions... I will not let him off lightly, Lawson! Tell me, how would you like him to be dealt with to settle this corporate grievance?\"","Jude didn’t hesitate for a single second. \"I want him in federal prison.\"","Maxwell Pierce’s expression changed drastically.","At this moment, Richard Pierce angrily pointed a finger at Jude. \"Lawson, don’t go too far! Donovan already knows he’s wrong, and your pop star wasn’t even harmed! We’re all corporate executives here, gentlemen; let’s settle this with a fine, don’t take it too far!\"","Jude’s eyes flashed with anger. \"Richard, listen to yourself! Am I going too far? It’s your pathetic son who went too far! He’s unworthy of his title!\"","Richard pleaded with the Chairman. \"Father, Donovan is the family’s legitimate heir! If he goes to federal prison and word gets out to the press, our studio becomes a joke! Our stock will plummet to zero. How could we ever hold our heads up again? Please, Father, reconsider!\"","Maxwell Pierce nodded, his shoulders slumping as he tried to persuade Jude. \"Lawson, his father has a valid point. This matter shouldn’t be made public to the federal authorities; this concerns the Pierce family’s reputation and our shareholder value. If this scandal spreads and causes an uproar, our current film distributions could unravel, and the international deals we’ve worked hard on will be wasted.\"","Jude fell silent for a moment.","A drawn-out federal trial would tie up Apex Media’s legal teams and drag Lyla’s name through the very tabloid mud Jude was trying to protect her from.","But he couldn’t just let Donovan off the hook...","Jude looked at the Chairman, his tone calm. \"I have a suggestion, Chairman, which you may consider. How about this: you expel Donovan from the Pierce family trust and strip him of all executive shares... remove him from this conglomerate! This matter need not be made public to the feds, but his total expulsion must be done today!\"","Jude’s suggestion was harsh.","\"If I can’t send him to federal prison without dragging my own artists into a media circus,\" Jude said, \"then expelling him into total poverty is a compromise I can accept. Either way, I want him removed from this industry. Just seeing him disgusts me.\"","Donovan was terrified, scrambling up from the carpet. \"Lawson, you’re going way too far! I’m the Pierce family’s oldest legitimate grandson; how can you demand my grandfather expel me so casually?!\"","\"I oppose this entirely!\" Richard shouted, slamming his fist on the table. \"Father, you can’t expel Donovan! He is the oldest legitimate grandson, and he will inherit the family’s assets in the future! Father, you must reconsider!\"","Maxwell Pierce found himself at a difficult loss.","However, at this moment, he had to give Jude Lawson a definitive explanation...","If Maxwell protected Donovan, Jude would undoubtedly launch a hostile takeover that would obliterate Pierce Studios overnight.","Maxwell Pierce found it incredibly difficult to make this final decision.","\"Chairman, is this decision so incredibly hard?\" Jude asked with a mocking smile. \"Expel Donovan from the family trust right now, and we will settle this corporate dispute quietly. Otherwise, I’ll have no choice but to call my contacts at the Department of Justice, as a federal prison sentence seems far more fitting for him.\"","\"Shut up, damn you! You arrogant Wall Street kid! Who the hell are you to speak to us like this?!\"","Richard Pierce pounced forward across the table.","In his blind fury, Richard lunged wildly to hit Jude.","Watching the studio executive rush at him with a raised fist, Jude laughed.","He thought how it couldn’t be blamed on him if this arrogant executive came at him on his own."]},{"number":42,"title":"Chapter 42: Powerless Trash","paragraphs":["Jude Lawson had just boldly suggested expelling Donovan Pierce from the family trust.","In a fit of blind rage, Richard Pierce lunged forward, attempting to slap Jude across the face.","Having his son’s future ruined by someone he utterly despised, Richard naturally couldn’t hold back his temper.","And with the deep sense of superiority in front of Jude, Richard believed that, as a senior executive of Pierce Studios, Jude would just obediently cower and take the beating.","As Richard’s bulky body closed in on Jude, a slap was just about to land squarely on Jude’s face.","Jude gently sidestepped, his movements impossibly fast, and Richard swung at empty air.","Due to the uncontrolled force of his own swing, the senior executive nearly fell face-first onto the carpet.","\"How dare you dodge me!\" Richard shouted angrily, his face flushed red as he turned around and charged at Jude again.","Jude frowned slightly, watching the charging executive.","Without a moment’s hesitation, Jude raised his leg and kicked Richard squarely in the belly, sending the man tumbling backward.","Richard hit the nearby boardroom table, scattering documents and finally stopping his momentum.","Jude stepped forward, grabbed Richard by the neck of his shirt, and lifted the bulky executive straight off the floor like a helpless chicken.","With only a slight application of force from Jude’s hand, Richard found it impossible to breathe, his face turning a bruised red as fear overwhelmed him.","The entire executive boardroom fell silent. Everyone was stunned.","He had lifted Richard Pierce off the ground with just one single hand!","\"Lawson, let him go!\" Chairman Maxwell Pierce shouted in alarm. He had to intervene before someone was killed.","But Jude ignored the Chairman. Holding Richard’s neck in a vice-like grip, Jude leaned in and said coldly, \"So, Richard, do you still want to fight?\"","Richard’s limbs struggled, kicking wildly at the air, but he couldn’t break free of Jude’s grip, looking exactly like a rabbit facing its inevitable death.","If this chokehold continued for another ten seconds, he really would die right there in the boardroom.","Richard hurriedly gasped out, \"I won’t... dare again.\"","\"Try moving against me again, and I’ll kill you,\" Jude said, tossing Richard aside like discarded trash.","Richard fell to the ground like a dead dog, struggling to get up, gulping for oxygen.","His throat bore the distinct imprint of Jude’s five fingers. With Jude’s unnatural strength, crushing his neck would have seemed an incredibly easy task.","Seeing this display, every single executive in the room was frightened.","Their previous gazes of corporate disdain towards Jude turned somewhat fearful and deeply cautious.","Only then did Jude adjust his cuffs, turn to Maxwell Pierce, and say smoothly, \"Chairman, you saw it too. He was far too ashamed of his son’s actions and angrily wanted to hit me first. I was merely acting in standard self-defense.\"","Sweat dripped from every executive’s brow.","\"Ahem,\" Maxwell cleared his throat nervously, trying to smooth things over. \"We’re all civilized executives here. Let’s talk things out professionally. Both of you must keep calm.\"","Jude smiled slightly and looked down at Richard. \"The Chairman is right. If we can reason things out like businessmen, let’s not fight in the boardroom. I sincerely apologize for my earlier actions.\"","Richard, still shaken and gasping for air on the floor, was angry and thoroughly startled, unwilling to let it go that easily.","But seeing Jude politely apologize, he simply snorted and clutched his bruised throat, not daring to retaliate.","Everyone at the table noticed that Jude possessed a remarkably broad mind, perfectly able to switch between violence and diplomacy, in stark contrast to the petty Richard.","They couldn’t help but drastically change their overall opinion of the young billionaire.","\"Chairman, why don’t we finally get back to the main issue at hand?\" Jude said, resting his hands on the back of a chair. \"I cannot forgive what Donovan did to my lead artist. He either leaves Pierce Studios right now, or he goes to a federal prison. The final decision is yours, Chairman.\"","Jude looked around the table. \"Give the Chairman some time to think,\" Jude said to the room at large. \"This matter concerns the studio’s destiny on the stock market. To this conglomerate, Donovan is just a piece of rotten garbage. I believe Chairman Pierce will make the right choice.\"","Everyone simply looked at Maxwell Pierce, anxiously awaiting his executive decision.","Donovan was incredibly anxious, pleading from his knees, \"Grandfather, you can’t listen to him! I’m the sole legitimate heir of Pierce Studios! Please don’t drive me away from the company!\"","Maxwell Pierce was silent for a long moment, then finally sighed, his age showing on his face, and said, \"Donovan’s actions are truly heinous, causing great harm to the family’s reputation. This cannot be forgiven. As of today, Donovan is permanently expelled from the Pierce family trust and stripped of all executive shares. Unless he miraculously gains the total forgiveness of Apex Media, especially Lyla, he will never be allowed to step foot into Pierce Studios again!\"","\"Grandfather, no!\"","Donovan cried out in utter despair, his face deathly pale, as if struck by lightning, his very soul terrified.","His grandfather had actually expelled him from the family trust permanently!","Maxwell closed his eyes tightly, ignoring Donovan’s wails. Expelling his most beloved grandson made him feel terrible, but he had no other choice in the face of Jude’s leverage.","Not to mention the threat of a federal investigation, if he continued to protect Donovan in such criminal matters, the entire Pierce board would be dissatisfied, and his image as the respected Chairman would completely collapse.","Seeing that pleading with his grandfather was entirely futile, Donovan turned to the other executives at the table, \"Say something! Plea for me! Didn’t you all always try to please me before this?! Why are you all completely silent now?!\"","However, the other members of the Pierce board remained silent, exchanging nervous glances, and no one pleaded for Donovan.","Now, however, Donovan was officially nothing more than powerless trash...","Seeing this total betrayal, Donovan laughed angrily, pointing a shaking finger at everyone and swore, \"You pack of greedy ingrates! You’re all damn ingrates!\"","\"Enough!\"","Maxwell Pierce’s expression turned remarkably grim. \"You are no longer part of this studio. Someone, take Donovan out!\"","Several security guards quickly came over, lifting Donovan by the arms, pulling him away from the table.","Naturally, Donovan refused to leave quietly, struggling against the guards, howling like a ghost.","Even the two security guards had significant difficulty controlling his thrashing..."]},{"number":43,"title":"Chapter 43: The Event","paragraphs":["Later that week, the annual Global Media Symposium was held in the grand ballroom of the city’s most exclusive luxury hotel.","It was a formal corporate event attended by the most powerful executives in the entertainment and financial sectors.","In a VIP corner of the ballroom, a tense standoff was occurring.","\"Do you have any idea who I am?\"","Cassandra stood up from the velvet lounge chair, crossing her arms tightly.","\"Cassandra, wasn’t it? You just introduced yourself a moment ago, didn’t you?\" Harper replied, swirling the champagne in her crystal flute.","*This Cassandra woman must really have a few screws loose,* Harper thought to herself, unimpressed.","\"You! I am Chairman Sterling’s personal secretary!\" Cassandra snapped.","Harper raised an eyebrow, a mocking smile touching her lips. *Chairman Sterling’s personal secretary, eh?*","\"Does your Chairman’s wife actually know you’re attending this exclusive corporate symposium with your dear Chairman Sterling today?\" Harper asked.","\"What’s that got to do with you?!\" Cassandra shrieked, her face turning crimson.","\"You’re right, it’s not my business at all,\" Harper said with a wave of her hand.","She glanced over her shoulder at the armed private military contractor standing in the shadows. \"Ghost, take her back to Chairman Sterling and tell him he shouldn’t let every stray dog off its leash at a gala. If it bites someone important, he’s the one who’ll be held entirely responsible.\"","\"Yes, Ms. Harper!\"","This time, Ghost gave Cassandra no time to react.","He stepped forward with terrifying speed, grabbed her by the belt of her designer dress, and hoisted her straight into the air like a piece of mislaid luggage.","Ghost remained unfazed by her screaming, his eyes scanning the dense crowd for the man who had brought Cassandra to the symposium: Chairman Sterling.","Ghost quickly located Chairman Sterling holding court near the ice sculptures.","He strode over with long steps, still carrying the squirming Cassandra, and dropped her directly beside the Chairman’s shoes.","\"Chairman Sterling,\" Ghost said, his voice a deep rumble. \"My superior has a message for you: ’You shouldn’t let every stray dog off its leash. If it bites someone, you’re the one who will be held responsible.’\"","\"Who the hell was that?!\"","Chairman Sterling asked furiously, looking at the other executives around him.","After a long moment, a junior executive in the crowd spoke up hesitantly, pointing a shaking finger across the ballroom. \"I think I saw him come from that direction, Chairman. It’s significantly less crowded over there in the VIP alcove. I think only Jude Lawson’s elite group went to sit there for a bit. Now, the only one left in the alcove is the young female executive who came in with them.\"","Chairman Sterling turned to the speaker, his eyes narrowing. \"Are you sure?\"","If that was actually the case, then this young female executive was certainly not someone to be trifled with lightly.","\"If you’re concerned about the optics, Chairman Sterling, you could go over and see for yourself,\" another CEO chimed in, swirling his scotch. \"Didn’t you say your daughter has quite the intimate relationship with that young Wall Street titan of the Lawson family?\"","Hearing them explicitly mention his daughter and Jude Lawson in the same breath, Chairman Sterling proudly puffed out his chest, his anger replaced by immense pride.","That supposed Ivy League connection was his ultimate trump card, the very thing that allowed him to feel a cut above everyone else in this crowded ballroom.","Chairman Sterling’s imposing group of executives looked like they were spoiling for a corporate fight.","In direct response to the approaching threat, the seven armed members of Ghost’s private security detail, who had been blending into the crowd, suddenly materialized out of nowhere and formed a circular ring around Harper.","\"Are you the woman who just had an unprovoked run-in with Cassandra?\"","Chairman Sterling hadn’t forgotten that it was specifically on this woman’s orders that a bodyguard had just dragged his secretary over to him in front of his peers.","Harper had just done a quick search on her encrypted phone for key figures at the Sterling Media company, so she’d seen Chairman Sterling’s online profile. She knew the arrogant man leading the group at the front was its Chairman.","\"Has Chairman Sterling come over here to hold me strictly accountable for my actions?\" Harper asked, remaining seated in her chair.","\"I am the one who brought Cassandra here tonight,\" Chairman Sterling declared, ensuring the surrounding crowd heard him. \"Even if you have some tangential business connection to Jude Lawson and his financial circle, that gives you no right to be so incredibly insolent to my personal secretary.\"","\"However,\" Chairman Sterling continued, adopting a magnanimous tone, \"seeing as you’re still very young and inexperienced, I’m willing to let this entire matter drop right now if you just stand up and apologize to Cassandra.\"","Hearing Chairman Sterling’s absurd words, Harper simply stared at him over the rim of her champagne flute as if he were a complete moron.","\"Chairman Sterling, what is the exact meaning of this? Did you bring this whole crowd over to my alcove to cause trouble for my President?\"","Before Harper could even say a single word in her own defense, Jude Lawson’s voice cut through the ballroom from behind Chairman Sterling’s entourage. Everyone hurriedly turned to look.","\"Mr. Lawson!\" Chairman Sterling beamed, his anger vanishing as he stepped forward to the billionaire. \"I’m Chairman Sterling, and my daughter is Vanessa Sterling. I’d like to take this public opportunity to thank you so very much for taking such intimate care of my daughter while you two were at Harvard Business School together.\"","Harper slowly lowered her champagne flute, shooting Jude a skeptical look that clearly said: *You took care of Vanessa Sterling at school?*","\"Chairman Sterling, I’m afraid there’s been a misunderstanding on your part,\" Jude said. \"I wasn’t particularly close with any female students during my university days at Harvard, let alone in a financial or social position to ’take care’ of anyone.\"","Chairman Sterling was dumbfounded.","What the hell was happening?","At home, his daughter Vanessa had always claimed that Jude Lawson had looked after her quite well while they were studying in Cambridge!","How could the billionaire now be saying he wasn’t close to any female students?!","\"Mr. Lawson, my daughter’s name is Vanessa Sterling. She told me you were always very kind to her when you were studying abroad!\" Chairman Sterling said, trying to jog Jude’s memory of his daughter to save face. \"Vanessa never lies to me!\""]},{"number":44,"title":"Chapter 44: Sugar Daddy","paragraphs":["\"Then you’ve probably been deceived by your own daughter,\" Jude replied. \"I don’t recall interacting with anyone named Vanessa Sterling from my time studying in Cambridge.\"","Jude actually remembered the girl, but their relationship could hardly be called close in any sense of the word...","However, he hadn’t known that Vanessa Sterling would actually blatantly lie to Chairman Sterling just to elevate her own status.","\"Now, shall we discuss exactly why Chairman Sterling brought so many senior executives here to this specific alcove? What did you realistically hope to accomplish?\"","Jude glanced coldly over Chairman Sterling and the large group of executives standing nervously behind him.","Though Jude wore a faint smile, it sent an immediate chill down the spine of every man present.","\"A misunderstanding, Mr. Lawson! It’s all a massive misunderstanding! We just came over... to say a polite hello to Ms. Harper,\" Chairman Sterling stammered.","\"We just heard from Cassandra that Ms. Harper is your primary executive, Mr. Lawson, so we came over to familiarize ourselves with her. We wanted to formally avoid any accidental offenses in the future... wouldn’t want to step on our own industry partners, after all!\" another CEO chimed in, trying to save face.","\"So you came over here to say hello to me?\" Harper asked from her chair, swirling her champagne. \"Is forcing someone to publicly apologize to a mistress your standard way of greeting people in the media sector? How... unique.\"","\"Yes! An apology!\" Chairman Sterling latched onto the word like a lifeline. \"Cassandra! Get over here and apologize to Ms. Harper right this instant!\"","Harper sat on the sofa, watching Cassandra with a sharp smile that wasn’t quite a smile.","\"Ms. Cassandra, you don’t look very well at all. Are you unhappy with this arrangement?\" Harper asked.","\"Not at all! Ms. Harper, my apologies,\" Cassandra muttered, looking down at the carpet.","\"What was that? Your voice is far too quiet, I can’t hear you over the music.\"","\"My apologies, Ms. Harper!\"","Cassandra raised her voice, but her made-up expression was still full of burning resentment.","\"I just had Ghost call Mrs. Sterling,\" Harper said, taking a sip of her champagne. \"Ms. Cassandra, what do you think of this little present?\"","Harper’s statement made Chairman Sterling immediately break out in a sweat.","\"Ms. Harper, you...\"","Chairman Sterling wanted to accuse Harper of fighting dirty, but he had just started to speak when a warning look from Jude Lawson stopped him dead in his tracks.","\"If there’s nothing else to discuss, you may all leave my alcove,\" Jude ordered.","No matter how deeply resentful Chairman Sterling and Cassandra were in that moment, they had no choice but to drop it and retreat.","Although the other executives were incredibly eager to see what would happen next, Jude Lawson had explicitly spoken, so they couldn’t very well keep lingering around the VIP area.","One by one, they quickly made their nervous excuses and scattered back into the ballroom...","Once everyone was finally gone, Harper set her champagne down and looked up at Jude and the advisors. \"So, what were your results in the VIP lounge?\"","Jude shook his head slightly, unbuttoning his suit jacket and sitting down. \"It’s not decided yet. We might have to wait another two days.\"","\"I thought with all four of you going in to negotiate, one of you would have been able to confidently land it,\" Harper said, slightly surprised.","\"Talented founders always have more options on the table,\" Jude replied calmly.","...","Twenty minutes after receiving a brief phone call and a series of photos from Ghost proving her husband’s blatant infidelity, Chairman Sterling’s wife stormed into the grand ballroom.","When Chairman Sterling and Cassandra saw Mrs. Sterling marching past the ice sculptures, the very look of panic in their eyes betrayed their deeply guilty consciences.","Meanwhile, Harper was gleefully watching the spectacular show from the sidelines of the alcove.","\"Harper, you did significantly more than just have Ghost make a phone call, didn’t you?\" Director Vance noted, chuckling softly.","\"Hmm... I think there were probably... some surveillance photos attached, too? I’m very thorough with my corporate communications, after all,\" Harper smiled innocently.","Director Vance stealthily gave Harper a thumbs-up from his chair.","\"This year’s media conference is certainly incredibly lively,\" another advisor noted.","The advisor picked up a piece of expensive melon from the catering table and took a bite with great, highly amused relish.","Director Vance toyed with the expensive watch on his wrist, his expression also full of deep meaning.","Jude Lawson peeled a seedless grape and handed it to Harper.","\"Sterling! How dare you cheat on me behind my back?!\"","Mrs. Sterling, holding a stack of glossy photos she’d had rush-printed at the hotel’s business center, threw them right at Chairman Sterling’s chest, sending them scattering all across the ballroom floor.","\"Whoa! It looks like there’s more than one woman in these photos!\"","A nosy media executive glanced down at the glossy photos on the floor, and sure enough, someone had instantly discovered the real, devastating gist of the leak.","\"And you! You shameless, pathetic hussy!\" Mrs. Sterling screamed, turning her wrath on Cassandra. \"Of all the wealthy people to blindly seduce, you specifically go after a married man! Are you that desperate for a sugar daddy that you’ll even eat someone else’s leftovers?!\"","*PFFT!*","Mrs. Sterling’s scathing words were quite funny to the corporate crowd, and many prominent executives couldn’t hold in their sudden bursts of laughter.","Cassandra’s face was a sickly color.","She didn’t verbally refute a single one of Mrs. Sterling’s screaming accusations; she just stood there paralyzed with her head lowered.","Anyone who didn’t know the absolute truth might have thought Mrs. Sterling was the one unfairly bullying her.","\"Honey, please, this is a misunderstanding! Let’s talk about it at home,\" Chairman Sterling begged, sweating profusely. \"Do you really want everyone here in the industry to laugh at our family’s expense?\"","Chairman Sterling was drowning in crushing regret.","He never should have brought Cassandra tonight...","If he hadn’t arrogantly brought her, he wouldn’t have offended Harper.","If he hadn’t offended Harper, none of this digital surveillance would have ever come to light!","\"A misunderstanding?! With all these crystal-clear photos right here on the floor, you’re actually telling me it’s a misunderstanding?!\" Mrs. Sterling roared.","\"A misunderstanding that you had your hands around those junior employees’ waists?! A misunderstanding that you were kissing them in the elevators?! Or a misunderstanding that you were embracing in public?!\"","\"Sterling! Everything you have right now, you have because my family’s trust fund supported you! Believe it or not, the exact same way I made you a corporate success, I can grind you right back into the dirt!\"","*Wow. I never would have guessed there was this kind of juicy gossip between Chairman Sterling and his wife,* Harper thought.","Harper sat in her seat, listening with great, interest as the Sterling Media empire began to publicly implode.","\"Aren’t you going to do something about her?\"","Director Vance leaned over and looked at Jude Lawson."]},{"number":45,"title":"Chapter 45: Trouble at the Gate","paragraphs":["Across the city, in the backstreets of the financial district...","After Donovan Pierce was officially and publicly kicked out of the Pierce family trust, he wandered the streets of the financial district.","Logically, as a totally discarded member of the Pierce legacy, he possessed no corporate value, and no one on Wall Street would care about him anymore.","However, as he walked past a dark alleyway, Donovan was suddenly shoved into an unmarked black van and kidnapped.","Donovan was scared out of his wits.","A canvas bag was yanked forcefully over his head, blocking his vision, and he could only feel the vehicle jolting over the city potholes.","\"Who the hell are you people?! Let me go!\" Donovan screamed, his voice cracking. \"I’m the eldest son of the Pierce family, and you dare kidnap me?!\"","He received no answer, only a shove back against the floor.","\"Jude Lawson, did you get your security to take revenge on me, you bastard?!\" Donovan cried out blindly. \"Or was it Lyla?! Please, let me go! I have nothing left! *Sob... sob...*\"","Later, Donovan was roughly dragged into an industrial room and was forcibly sat down on a chair.","His head covering was then abruptly removed, revealing a person smiling bitterly at him.","\"Little Donovan, do you still recognize me?\" the person asked.","Donovan blinked against the overhead light, saw this person, and was stunned, showing an expression of profound surprise... this was someone he never, ever would have thought of.","Donovan blurted out, \"You... could it be... Gregory Vance?!\"","***","Meanwhile, across the city, Harper and Jude Lawson left the Pierce Studios headquarters, planning to head back to their own corporate home base at Apex Media.","Harper was driving her vintage car, and she stole a quiet glance at Jude resting in the passenger seat, blushing faintly as she said, \"Jude, I really haven’t thanked you enough for today; our studio’s safety was all thanks to your intervention.\"","Jude smiled faintly and said, \"No need to thank me, Harper; dismantling their board wasn’t much effort.\"","Jude looked out the window and smiled. \"Donovan Pierce has already been kicked out of the Pierce family, and the financial threat to our market share has been entirely resolved. In the media sector, no one should be able to aggressively shake your position as President anymore. As for me, my direct intervention is probably useless to you now. If you want to cash out your executive equity and terminate your contract, you can bring it up anytime.\"","Harper: \"...\"","She had just started having those deeply loyal, permanent thoughts, and Jude’s words were like a bucket of ice water poured over her head.","She could only nod, gripping the steering wheel. \"Okay, if this war is over, we can discuss my severance.\"","Jude made a nonchalant sound of agreement, and said nothing more on the subject.","He genuinely didn’t care much; he didn’t possess deep romantic feelings for Harper...","Elevating her and protecting her studio was purely a system task to expand his empire.","[Ding!]","Suddenly, Jude heard the familiar system sound clearly in his mind.","[Congratulations to the host for helping Apex Media resolve the Pierce Conglomerate financial threat.]","[You have received: $10,000,000 USD!]","Jude smiled wryly. The system still hadn’t changed its baseline metric...","All the standard milestone rewards invariably turned into ten million dollars in liquid cash.","She suddenly thought of something that had been bothering her and curiously asked, \"By the way, I’ve always wanted to ask you: you’re so incredibly wealthy and skilled, why do you personally intervene in these street-level conflicts? You could actually just hire a hundred elite mercenaries to do your dirty work.\"","Jude shifted his attention away from the system interface and said, \"Like what?\"","\"I’m not interested in hiding behind a wall of bodyguards.\"","Harper asked softly, \"Then why did you agree to elevate me to President and help me build this studio in the first place?\"","Jude said, his tone flat, \"Weren’t you the one who pleaded with me in the lobby to give you a chance? I was just feeling softhearted...\"","\"Alright.\" Harper sighed, feeling a bit hurt by the answer.","This guy truly didn’t seem to have any emotional interest in her whatsoever...","It was like he was just going through the corporate motions because it was a task.","Could it actually be that her personal charm wasn’t enough?","Suddenly, she had a shocking thought; *Oh my god, could it be that he’s not actually into women...*","In the blink of an eye, Harper noticed Jude’s sharp gaze fixed intently outside the car window, as if actively admiring something on the sidewalk.","Harper curiously asked, \"What are you looking at?\"","Jude pointed ahead with his tailored hand and smiled faintly. \"See that girl walking out of the boutique on the corner? Wow, what an incredible figure. Probably a perfect D-cup...\"","Harper almost swerved and fainted against the steering wheel; *Damn it, he was checking out street beauties!* This proves he’s normal...","Harper was flustered.","In no time, they safely arrived at the towering Apex Media headquarters.","Director Vance and Maya were both waiting anxiously in the executive lobby for their return.","\"Thank heaven you’re alright, Harper,\" Maya ran over and hugged the young President tightly.","Harper smiled warmly and said, \"Maya, I’m fine, thanks to Jude.\"","Director Vance was much more straightforward, smiling broadly as he stepped forward. \"Mr. Lawson, I’ve heard about exactly what you did at Pierce Studios. I didn’t expect you to be so aggressively capable in a confrontation; Harper escaping this corporate disaster was all thanks to you. On behalf of the entire Apex family, I thank you.\"","Jude smiled and said smoothly, \"Director Vance, no need to be polite. She’s my appointed President; of course I have to protect her assets.\"","Director Vance paused, nodded deeply, and said, \"I think I might be starting to fully understand exactly why Harper is so fiercely loyal to you.\"","Harper blushed. \"Director Vance, what are you talking about?\"","Director Vance smiled knowingly. \"Mr. Lawson may be a Wall Street titan, but he has an unshakeable sense of responsibility for his people. Harper must have seen this in you from day one.\"","Although the system task was officially completed, since Harper hadn’t actually brought up terminating her contract, Jude continued to use Apex Media as his primary home base.","On this particular day, as usual, Jude’s Maybach cruised back to the corporate estate.","Suddenly, a loud commotion up ahead at the main gates caught Jude’s attention."]},{"number":46,"title":"Chapter 46: Hostage Situation","paragraphs":["That evening, as usual, Jude Lawson had instructed his driver to pull the Maybach up to the edge of the high-end commercial plaza just outside the Apex Media headquarters.","Because of a police barricade blocking the main avenue, Jude decided to step out and walk the remaining distance to the executive tower.","Every single time he appeared in public among the old-money elites, he attracted strange, fearful, and resentful looks from the rival executives and socialites.","Not many good words came out of their mouths.","\"Look, isn’t that the Wall Street vulture who just dismantled Pierce Studios?\"","\"Apex Media may not find his hostile tactics shameful, but I certainly do!\"","Jude heard these whispered remarks every single day, and after hearing them enough, he had gotten entirely used to the predictable jealousy of inferior competitors.","Jude pretended not to hear the whispers, walking with steady steps through the upscale community plaza.","Suddenly, there was a commotion in front of a modern glass building; it turned out a large group of panicked pedestrians had gathered in front of an upscale corner convenience store, and something dangerous seemed to have just happened.","\"Oh my god, that person is crazy, how could he not even spare a little girl?!\"","The crowd was buzzing with fearful discussion.","At the exact same time, a marked police cruiser was parked diagonally outside the shattered glass doors of the convenience store.","A few uniformed police officers lined up behind the cruiser doors, one of them holding a megaphone, shouting towards the dark inside of the store.","\"Suspect inside, listen up, the police have surrounded you. We strongly hope you surrender immediately, and release the hostage. Resisting us will do you absolutely no good.\"","The senior officer shouted until his voice was hoarse, but there was no response from inside the store; no one spoke.","However, the frightened cries of a little girl could be heard echoing from the aisles.","It seemed someone inside had taken a little girl hostage!","An elderly auntie, likely a direct relative of the little girl, knelt on the pavement crying, her face full of heart-wrenching fear, \"You heartless monster! Let go of my granddaughter, please don’t hurt her!\"","At this exact moment, another armored police SUV arrived on the scene, its sirens blaring.","A female tactical officer got out of the armored car.","Jude recognized her instantly from the warehouse incident reports; it was Captain Olivia Reed!","\"Captain Reed!\"","Seeing Captain Reed finally arrive, the stressed officers relaxed, as if their ultimate tactical savior had finally arrived on the chaotic scene.","Captain Reed immediately unholstered her sidearm and asked, \"What’s the exact situation here?\"","The senior officer who had been shouting through the megaphone quickly explained, \"Here’s what happened, Captain: today we received an anonymous tip-off about an illegal narcotics ring operating in this sector. Our undercover colleagues came to investigate and indeed found the prime suspect. When the suspect was discovered, he panicked and fled, and was chased into this convenience store where he took a little girl hostage.\"","Captain Reed frowned deeply; taking an innocent little girl hostage in a public space is an incredibly serious matter that must not go wrong.","Captain Reed asked, \"Does the suspect have any firearms or weapons?\"","\"He has a serrated tactical knife,\" the officer replied grimly. \"Moreover, he’s quite skilled in close-quarters combat; our pursuit team couldn’t catch him in the alley, and he managed to fight his way into the store. Now that he has taken hostages at knifepoint, we don’t dare to recklessly rush in for fear of harming them.\"","\"Cops outside, listen up! I’ll give you exactly ten seconds! Drop your damn guns and back up three hundred meters! Follow my orders! I have two people here; killing one of them is no big deal to me!\"","A frantic man’s voice echoed from the depths of the store, the suspect finally speaking up to negotiate.","Captain Reed took the megaphone from the officer and said firmly, \"Suspect inside, I’m Captain Reed, the officer in charge here. I hope you don’t do anything stupid to harm the hostages!\"","The man chuckled darkly, a crazed edge to his voice. \"So it’s a female cop in charge! Do exactly as I say obediently!\"","Captain Reed said, \"No problem at all, you can come out safely now.\"","Captain Reed didn’t hesitate for a second. \"Do exactly as he says!\"","The officers reluctantly threw their guns down onto the asphalt and retreated, indeed moving back a full three hundred meters to the edge of the plaza.","Captain Reed also backed away slowly, calling out to the dark store, \"Suspect inside, we’ve put down our guns and retreated fully as you demanded. You can come out now.\"","But there was only silence inside, with no suspect appearing in the doorway.","\"Hmph!\"","An angry grunt came from inside the aisles, \"You actually think you can fool me, female cop?! You all are clearly up to something, don’t think you can trick me into coming out into the open!\"","Captain Reed was sweating under her vest, \"You’re overthinking it! We only want the hostages safe, we really have no other hidden intentions. You can come out assured.\"","The man shouted back, \"I believe you, liar! You’re full of bad ideas, probably got sniper bullets ready for my head right now! As soon as I step out, I’ll be sniped! Don’t think I haven’t seen enough cop movies to know the drill?!\"","\"You really want to save the hostages, huh?! I won’t let you succeed! I’ll kill a hostage first right now to prove I’m serious, this little girl it is!\"","Captain Reed was incredibly anxious; this suspect was agitated and paranoid, likely hard to control through standard negotiation.","She wanted to draw her backup weapon, rush in, and stop him before blood was shed.","But she simply couldn’t do that; the risk to the child was far too great...","Just then, suddenly, someone beside the police barricade moved swiftly, like a lethal arrow fired off a taut string, darting into the convenience store, doing exactly what Captain Reed wanted to do.","\"Oh my god, he’s going to die!\"","Everyone in the plaza was shocked; a civilian rushing in at this volatile time was bound to end badly for him.","In stark contrast to the terrified onlookers, Captain Reed’s face showed immense surprise and delight.","Though the rush was incredibly quick, she recognized immediately that the billionaire CEO, Jude Lawson, was the one who had darted into the store!","As Jude rushed in, an angry man’s voice came from the back of the store, \"You actually dare to come in here... ah!\"","He had barely begun cursing Jude when the threat suddenly turned into a horrific scream of agony."]},{"number":47,"title":"Chapter 47: Sun From the West","paragraphs":["This scene happened so fast that even the trained police officers were stunned.","The situation was exactly this: the suspect was hiding deep in the aisles of the convenience store, holding a little girl and the female clerk hostage at knifepoint. The armed police couldn’t just go in, and it wasn’t easy for the SWAT snipers to aim through the cluttered window displays. Captain Reed’s original idea was to carefully lure the suspect out first.","At this critical moment, Jude Lawson actually rushed in, unexpected by everyone in the plaza...","The suspect cursed upon seeing Jude, but suddenly let out a horrific scream.","Then, a chilling sound of bones breaking could be clearly heard from inside the store.","*Bam!*","Suddenly, an adult man flew out of the convenience store, breaking the door open, and landed in front of the police barricade like a dead dog.","Everyone in the plaza was stunned, watching him fall to the ground.","Captain Reed reacted quickly, drawing her service gun and sternly shouting, \"Don’t move!\"","Her worry was unnecessary...","The person couldn’t move at all; his knife hand was clearly broken.","The jagged bone had actually pierced the skin, seemingly snapped by someone with terrifying strength.","Everyone in the crowd was frightened pale. It was absolutely terrifying!","The police rushed forward and handcuffed the suspect to the pavement.","Just then, Jude Lawson walked out of the shattered doors holding a little girl, followed closely by a pale-faced convenience store clerk.","The hostages were unharmed.","Everyone collectively breathed a sigh of relief.","Jude Lawson was amazing, rushing in and taking down the armed suspect in such an incredibly short time, not giving the suspect any chance whatsoever to react!","Especially the police, the trained tactical professionals, they knew exactly how difficult this maneuver was...","For a long moment, they looked at Jude as if he were a literal deity.","This young billionaire was incredible, handling such a formidable person barehanded in the absolute blink of an eye!","\"Hey, isn’t this the Wall Street vulture who just bought out Apex Media?\"","\"The corporate raider?!\"","\"It’s him!\"","The wealthy residents and rival executives of the commercial community recognized Jude at this moment and started discussing in surprise.","Jude brought the little girl in front of the elderly Auntie, who was emotionally overwhelmed and had fainted just now, but had now been resuscitated by paramedics.","Seeing the little girl safely rescued from the knife, she was overjoyed.","First thing, the Auntie checked the little girl over. Finding her unharmed, she breathed a sigh of relief.","Immediately, the elderly Auntie knelt down on the pavement before Jude.","\"Young man, thank you so much for saving my granddaughter, really, truly thank you. Juan’er, thank your savior quickly,\" the Auntie said gratefully through her tears.","The little girl sniffled and said, \"Thank you, mister.\"","Jude smiled warmly. \"No need to thank me, I was just passing by, it was just a small lift.\"","The police officers were instantly drenched in sweat; *just a small lift?!*","He really thought anyone could do it, he was far too casual!","How could this billionaire leave them any tactical face?!","\"Sister Fang, what exactly happened here?\"","At this moment, a voice spoke from the crowd.","It was Victoria Vance, the Senior Legal Counsel for Apex Media, holding a box of files, coming over with a surprised look.","Sister Fang held Victoria’s hand with immense gratitude, \"Victoria, Juan’er was kidnapped by a criminal just now, and it was entirely thanks to your new CEO who bravely saved her! Your CEO is so incredibly good and really impressive, Apex Media is extremely lucky to have such a good, noble leader!\"","The commercial community’s elite residents also praised without ceasing...","\"Such a good, brave young man!\"","\"Really envy Victoria! Apex Media has great vision, finding such a capable CEO!\"","Everyone in the plaza gave a thumbs-up to Jude Lawson.","Victoria was stunned.","Did she actually hear correctly?","Everyone in the elite plaza was praising him, praising him until she felt a bit elated and proud.","Jude was supposed to be the shame of their studio, how did he suddenly seem to become their greatest pride?","\"Counselor Vance, what a coincidence. Let me do it.\"","Jude chuckled, taking the box of legal files from Victoria’s hands and tucking it under his arm.","\"Captain Reed, if there’s nothing else you need from me for the report, I’ll go back to the boardroom and get to work first.\"","Jude said to the police nearby, then turned his shoulders and said, \"Counselor Vance, it’s a bit of a walk back to the executive tower, shall I give you an escort?\"","Hearing the elite neighbors say this, Victoria couldn’t possibly refuse Jude’s polite offer...","If she declined, wouldn’t it instantly make her seem ungrateful, refusing such a good leader?","The wealthy neighbors would criticize her endlessly.","She didn’t say much, just walked proudly by his side.","Jude quickly set a steady pace, leaving the crime scene.","He had to leave quickly; Captain Reed was still on the scene. He didn’t want to explain his terrifying strength so much to the SWAT commander.","Earlier, Captain Reed was busy handling the suspect.","Now that the suspect had been securely taken away by the armored police car, Captain Reed finally found time to come and see Jude.","She saw Jude already walking far away, leaving only his broad silhouette.","Meanwhile, Jude escorted Victoria Vance, walking back to the estate.","Jude walked through the doors downstairs, carrying the box of files, and headed toward the private executive elevators with Victoria.","At this exact moment, Harper just returned from a meeting, driving her vintage car into the VIP garage.","She saw this scene through the lobby, and was stunned, thinking she was seeing things.","She didn’t see wrongly!","Her senior legal counsel actually returned happily to the office walking alongside Jude Lawson?!","Wasn’t Victoria always very much strictly against Jude’s methods? Did the sun actually rise from the west today?"]},{"number":48,"title":"Chapter 48: Raising the Stakes","paragraphs":["A few days later, inside Apex Media’s newly expanded esports division...","Dozens of nervous eyes shifted away from the glowing monitors, settling on the young billionaire standing at the back of the room.","Inside the newly renovated digital sports wing of Apex Media, a corporate standoff was brewing.","Ultimately, the decision of whether to accept this incredibly hostile exhibition match rested on Jude Lawson’s shoulders.","Right as the silence stretched to its breaking point, a familiar chime echoed in Jude’s mind.","[Objective: Eradicate the Vanguard faction’s arrogance in the digital arena. Demonstrate the superiority of Lawson Capital.]","[Requirement: Secure first place in the upcoming cross-studio exhibition match.]","[Reward upon completion: +2 Liquid Capital Sign-Ins, 1x High-Tier Corporate Asset Cache.]","Reading the interface hovering in his vision, Jude couldn’t help but let out a chilling laugh.","The system’s continuous influx of sign-in capital always arrived at the most opportune moments.","Without wasting a single second weighing the risks, Jude looked at the head coach of the gaming division. \"Accept the exhibition terms. If they are desperate to bleed money in a public lobby, we will gladly oblige them.\"","Jude adjusted his cuffs before adding, \"However, tell them a fifty-million-dollar wager is far too pathetic for my portfolio. If they genuinely want to make headlines today, bump the stakes to a flat one hundred million.\"","The gaming facility erupted into chaos. The professional athletes leaped out of their chairs, shouting with excitement.","Following Jude’s direct authorization, the facility manager immediately transmitted the escalated terms to the Vanguard executive offices.","Shockingly, the rival conglomerate accepted the nine-figure wager without a shred of hesitation.","The managing director of their gaming division, who was also the arrogant heir to the Vanguard empire, was personally leading his roster across town to the Apex facility right at this very moment.","They were coming to play a zero-ping exhibition match.","The stakes: One Hundred Million Dollars.","...","Barely thirty minutes later, the doors to the Apex training arena swung open.","Preston Vanguard strutted into the room, flanked by a entourage of coaches and more than a dozen backup players.","Dressed in exorbitant streetwear, the young heir carried a palpable aura of unearned superiority.","The moment Preston stepped onto the main floor, his gaze locked onto Jude.","He offered a sneer. \"You actually have the balls to risk a hundred million dollars against my roster, Lawson? Fine. I accept.\"","Preston crossed his arms. \"I can easily stomach a hundred-million-dollar loss. I just hope you don’t call your lawyers to void the contract when my boys humiliate you on your own servers.\"","The world-class players standing behind Jude immediately fired back on their CEO’s behalf.","\"Are you delusional, Preston? Mr. Lawson just dropped over a billion dollars to acquire our entire studio. Do you honestly think a hundred million means anything to him?\"","\"Keep acting tough, Preston! We all know Vanguard Media is bleeding quarterly revenue! When you lose this hundred million, you’re going to have to beg your daddy for a bailout!\"","The mockery from the Apex players caused Preston’s smug expression to darken into a vicious scowl.","\"What the hell gives you Apex losers the right to talk down to us?! You think getting bought out by some Wall Street suit magically makes you invincible?!\"","Preston laughed, stepping forward to close the distance.","He pointed a finger toward Jude’s chest. \"When I destroy Team Apex today, I’m going to make you realize what a catastrophic investment this buyout was.\"","\"The next global championship belongs to Vanguard. Today is simply a preview of your inevitable bankruptcy!\"","Preston’s arrogance stemmed from genuine confidence.","On the competitive ladder, Preston was universally recognized as a quasi-professional talent.","In the high-speed realm of competitive gaming, he feared no one...","Certain of his total victory, Preston maintained a cocky smirk as he introduced his starting lineup.","\"Since you’re about to lose a fortune, I’ll do you the courtesy of introducing the men who will take your money,\" Preston boasted, gesturing to his elite athletes. \"I brought my lethal Top-Lane specialist, our optimized Support, the best Jungler in the hemisphere, and a bot-lane carry.\"","Preston chuckled, tapping his own chest. \"As for the critical Core DPS role in the Mid-Lane? I’ll be taking that seat personally. I’m going to show you exactly how terrifying a fully integrated Vanguard roster can be!\"","Hearing Preston’s declaration, the five Apex champions turned to Jude, their faces flushed with fury.","\"Mr. Lawson, don’t let this spoiled brat intimidate you. We will obliterate them on the servers! The four of us, plus you in the fifth seat? I guarantee we’ll wipe the floor with them.\"","The Apex players stared down their rivals, eagerly waiting for Jude to finalize their battle strategy.","Jude allowed a smile to break across his face.","He was immensely satisfied by the unbridled hostility radiating from his newly acquired assets.","\"Since the Vanguard heir wants to play the hero, I’ll personally take the Mid-Lane Core DPS role.\"","\"Let’s see exactly how much his confidence is truly worth.\"","Preston burst into a fit of hysterical laughter.","Hearing that the stiff billionaire actually intended to duel him in the most demanding lane on the map was just too rich.","\"You? Dueling me in the Mid-Lane? That is genuinely the most pathetic thing I’ve ever heard!\" Preston wiped a tear from his eye. \"Let me educate you, Lawson. Even my own salaried champions admit that my spell-weaving is lethal!\"","Jude chuckled, turning his gaze toward the four Apex champions.","He cleared his throat. \"Before we log into the lobby, there is one minor financial adjustment I need to clarify.\"","Jude slid his hands into his pockets.","\"When you four gentlemen assist me in seizing Preston’s hundred million dollars today, I am going to liquidate fifty million of those winnings as a direct bonus.\"","\"The four of you will evenly split forty million dollars in liquid cash. The remaining ten million will be distributed evenly among the coaching and support staff.\"","The four professional athletes who were scheduled to play the match froze, their faces draining of color before flushing with hysteria.","\"Mr. Lawson... are you... are you serious?! If we win this single exhibition match, we each walk away with ten million dollars cash?!\"","\"Holy shit! That’s literally more than I’ve made in five years of global tournament prizes combined! Boss, we are going to murder them!\""]},{"number":49,"title":"Chapter 49: Protect the King","paragraphs":["The four contracted professional gamers on Team Apex were foaming at the mouth.","The promise of splitting forty million dollars in liquid cash had altered their brain chemistry.","\"Ten million a piece...\" the star Top-Laner muttered, his hands actually shaking as he gripped his mouse. \"Boss, I will literally die for you in this match!\"","\"If anyone on their squad even looks at your character model, I’m disconnecting their router,\" the Support player laughed manically. \"This is the greatest buyout in the history of e-sports!\"","Across the aisle, the rival athletes of Team Vanguard watched this ecstatic celebration with burning envy.","They were salaried professionals too, but their boss had never offered them anything close to a life-changing payout for a simple afternoon exhibition...","Sensing the morale of his own squad actively fracturing, Preston Vanguard gritted his teeth.","He couldn’t let Jude Lawson dominate the warfare before the keyboards even started clicking.","\"Don’t let this Wall Street suit buy your confidence!\" Preston shouted to his own players, his face flushed. \"If we secure this win today, I’ll authorize a twenty-million-dollar bonus pool! Ten million for the starting roster, and ten million for the coaching staff!\"","Preston puffed out his chest, waiting for the rapturous applause from his squad.","Instead, the Apex athletes immediately burst into laughter.","\"Are you serious right now, Preston?\" the Apex Jungler sneered. \"Your family’s conglomerate is allegedly worth billions, and you’re penny-pinching a twenty-million-dollar pool? Mr. Lawson just threw down fifty million without even blinking!\"","Preston’s face turned an ugly shade of crimson.","Sensing the collapse of Preston’s authority, Jude decided to drive the final nail into the coffin.","\"Let me be perfectly clear,\" Jude said. \"Regardless of whether we actually win or lose this digital exhibition, every single staff member in this room will receive a one-million-dollar performance bonus by the end of the day.\"","Jude checked his watch. \"Furthermore, I’ve already instructed my assistant to rent out the entirety of Le Bernardin tonight. The afterparty is fully covered.\"","The Apex coaching staff gasped in disbelief.","The Vanguard players stared across the room, looking miserable.","A few of them looked like they wanted to tear off their Vanguard jerseys and defect to Apex on the spot.","Comparing their cheap trust-fund heir to this endlessly generous Wall Street titan was just depressing...","\"Mr. Lawson, you have my loyalty,\" the Apex Support player swore, his voice deadly serious. \"If we somehow manage to lose this game after what you just did for us, I will retire from the professional circuit in shame.\"","\"We are going to rip them apart,\" the Top-Laner promise. \"They aren’t leaving this server alive.\"","Preston Vanguard felt sweat break out across his neck.","Unlike Jude, who viewed the hundred-million-dollar wager as mere pocket change compared to his system’s impending rewards, Preston had everything on the line.","\"Listen to me!\" Preston barked at his roster. \"My money is on the line here! You do not screw this up, do you hear me?! You play perfectly!\"","His screaming only served to stress his players out further, leaving them tense and miserable as they settled into their gaming chairs.","***","The game of choice was *Aetheria*, the globe’s premier competitive multiplayer battle arena...","Both CEOs sat at their keyboards, flanked by their world-class teammates.","Preston cracked his knuckles, pulling up the client login screen.","He typed in his credentials, a smirk returning to his face. \"Let me show you how actual gaming royalty logs in, Lawson.\"","The moment Preston authenticated his account, a server-wide notification flashed across the lobby in brilliant gold text, visible to everyone in the custom spectator room.","[GLOBAL VIP ALERT: Preston_Vanguard]","[The $10,000,000 Lifetime Whale Account has entered the lobby!]","The Vanguard coaching staff offered golf-clap applause.","\"A ten-million-dollar account,\" Preston boasted proudly. \"I bought the exclusive developer tier five years ago. It comes with custom entrance animations and priority server routing. This kind of digital real estate is strictly invite-only. A hundred million in cash can’t buy you this kind of verified clout.\"","It was a blatant display of wealth in the gaming community.","Jude reached out and tapped his enter key, authenticating the custom account his holding company had prepared for him earlier that morning.","The screens across the facility flashed a blinding crimson.","A server-wide alert overrode everything, accompanied by a deafening horn.","[Shareholder Prime — The $1,000,000,000 Lifetime Valuation Account has entered the lobby!]","[All servers bow to the Board of Directors!]","\"What... what the hell is that?!\" a Vanguard player whispered.","\"A one-billion-dollar valuation account?!\"","Preston’s jaw unhinged. He stared at Jude’s avatar in shock.","Humiliated before the match had even loaded, Preston remained dead silent, grinding his teeth in bitter rage.","He angrily locked in his character: an intense assassin designed for the Core DPS role.","*I’ll just have to murder him in the lane,* Preston thought viciously.","Jude selected his own champion... a late-game marksman designed for heavy DPS output.","He didn’t issue a single instruction to his team. He didn’t need to...","The moment Jude locked in his character, the four world-champion Apex players instantly adapted.","Abandoning their usual aggressive tournament strategies, they drafted the ultimate \"Protect the King\" composition.","The Top-Laner locked in a frontline tank with immense shielding capabilities.","The Jungler locked in a heavy-control vanguard designed exclusively to peel enemies away.","Both the Support and the secondary Bot-Laner locked in dedicated enchanter-healers, specialized in providing endless health regeneration, movement speed buffs, and defensive barriers.","These four masters of their craft were willingly throwing away all of their offensive pride, dedicating their skillsets to acting as Jude Lawson’s personal bodyguards.","The moment the loading screen vanished and the champions spawned into the fountain, a collective gasp echoed through the Vanguard training area.","Jude’s avatar was entirely unlike anything available in the standard client...","Instead of standard walking animations, Jude’s character levitated on a throne.","As the minions clashed in the center of the map, the laning phase began.","Preston’s fingers flew across his keyboard, dodging Jude’s slower projectiles and whittling down the billionaire’s health bar.","Smelling blood in the water, Preston saw his window of opportunity.","Jude was low on health and lingering close to the edge of his defensive turret.","Executing a lightning-fast combination of spells, Preston’s assassin dashed past the turret’s boundary, closing the gap to deliver the strike.","Suddenly, a champion leaped out of the nearby brush. It was the Apex Jungler!"]},{"number":50,"title":"Chapter 50: Pay to Win","paragraphs":["Before Preston could even register the ambush, his assassin was chained with three overlapping crowd-control abilities.","Suspended in the air, Preston watched in horror as Jude turned his throne around and executed Preston with a single critical strike.","[First Blood!]","\"What the hell?!\" Preston screamed, slamming his fist onto his desk. \"How is their Jungler already mid?! He hasn’t farmed a single neutral objective! Was he just sitting in that bush for three minutes?!\"","The Apex professional Jungler had abandoned his own progression, ignoring the rest of the map just to act as Jude’s invisible secret service agent.","Sitting across the room, Jude adjusted his gaming headset. \"I’m adding an extra million dollars to your final payout.\"","The Apex Jungler cheered so loudly the audio peaked. \"Thank you, Mr. Lawson! I’ll camp this lane until the servers shut down!\"","Hearing the CEO’s bribery, the other three Apex rioted on the communications channel, sick with jealousy.","\"I literally just lost a million dollars! I’m going to murder their bottom lane!\" the Support player wailed.","Preston, hearing the shouts echoing across the room, felt like he was genuinely losing his mind.","This was supposed to be a competitive exhibition of skill...","Instead, Jude Lawson was corrupting the sanctity of the arena, treating the map like his own personal Wall Street trading floor.","\"This is shameless!\" Preston yelled.","He pinged his own Vanguard Jungler. \"Get to the mid-lane right now! We are diving him together! I will not let this boomer disrespect me!\"","\"Understood, boss!\" the Vanguard Jungler replied. \"I’m flanking from the river now!\"","Respawning with a vengeance, Preston coordinated a two-man pincer attack.","As Jude stepped forward to claim a minion, Preston and his Jungler collapsed on the position.","Jude remained calm, utilizing a defensive dash to glide backward into the safety of his turret’s firing range.","Suddenly, the Vanguard Jungler seemingly panicked.","Instead of retreating from the ambush, the player \"accidentally\" missed his escape ability, tumbling far too deep under the orbital defense turret.","Trapped by the turret fire, the Vanguard Jungler stood still, allowing Jude to execute him.","[Double Kill!]","Preston stared at his screen, his brain short-circuiting...","He ripped off his headset and screamed across the Vanguard seating arrangement. \"Are you braindead?! What the hell was that dive?! You’re a salaried professional and you just walked under a turret and gave him a free bounty! Are you playing with your feet?!\"","Across the aisle, Jude chuckled darkly.","He leaned forward and typed a quick message into the global all-chat, visible to every single player.","[Shareholder Prime]: Incredible stunt work, Vanguard Jungler. Since your boss insists on abusing you for his own failures, I’ll gladly cover your hazard pay. One million dollars. DM me your routing number.*","Preston’s entire roster froze.","\"What... what is he typing?\" the Vanguard Support whispered in shock. \"He wants to reward our Jungler with a million dollars?\"","The Vanguard Jungler, however, was already moving...","Without hesitating for a fraction of a second, the professional quickly opened a private direct message channel to Jude’s account and typed in his offshore banking details.","Jude smiled. He picked up his phone from his desk, tapped into his holding company’s liquidity portal, and wired exactly one million dollars to the provided account.","Suddenly, the Vanguard Jungler’s personal cell phone vibrated on his desk.","He glanced down at the banking notification.","Preston saw the Jungler’s shaking hands and felt dread pool in his stomach.","His own player had just been financially assassinated in the middle of a live match...","\"You bastard!\" Preston roared. \"Everyone! Abandon your lanes! Top, Support, ADC! I want a full five-man rotation on the mid-lane right this second! I don’t care about the objectives, I don’t care about the turrets! I will not leave this room until I kill him at least once!\"","Sensing the incoming threat, the Apex communications channel erupted into a frenzy of greed.","\"Boss, they’re rotating!\" the Apex Top-Laner screamed, mashing his global teleport key. \"I’m coming in hot! Keep your wallet open, my million is secured!\"","The first teamfight of the exhibition match erupted in the center of the arena.","However, it was a slaughter...","The Vanguard roster was disjointed, stressed by their screaming boss, and operating with a Jungler who was sabotaging his own skill-shots.","The Top-Laner absorbed every single lethal projectile aimed at Jude.","The Support layered endless defensive shields over Jude’s character model. The Jungler pinned Preston to the floor.","Untouchable within his fortress of professional bodyguards, Jude rained down critical damage from his obsidian throne, melting the Vanguard roster into ash.","[TRIPLE KILL!]","As the announcer’s voice boomed through the facility, Jude laughed.","\"Clean execution, gentlemen.\" Jude said. \"Add another million dollars to everyone’s tab.","Preston Vanguard was having a meltdown...","Watching the first major objective slip through his fingers, he ripped off his designer headset and began eviscerating his own players.","\"You braindead amateurs!\" Preston roared, spittle flying from his lips. \"What the hell was that rotation?! You call yourselves salaried professionals?!\"","The four Vanguard athletes sat in silence, their eyes fixed on their monitors.","Listening to the pathetic tantrum across the room, Jude swirled a bottle of sparkling water and laughed softly.","Suddenly, Jude’s chat interface chimed.","It was another direct message from the Vanguard Jungler.","[Vanguard_Roamer]: Mr. Lawson, the rest of my roster is listening to this abuse on our comms. Our ADC, Support, and Top-Laner have had enough. If you are willing to cover their hazard pay, they will gladly deliver you the victory right now.*","Jude’s smile widened. He didn’t waste time typing a long-winded response.","[Shareholder Prime]: Provide their offshore routing numbers. One million dollars a head.*","Within thirty seconds, a rapid succession of banking credentials flooded Jude’s private message box.","He glanced over the top of his monitor at Preston Vanguard, who was still red-faced and screaming at his roster, oblivious to the fact that his team had just been bought out from under him.","Soon enough, a Preston forced his squad to regroup for a second, decisive engagement near the map’s primary neutral objective.","Given the gold deficit they had just suffered, this upcoming clash would undeniably decide the final outcome of the exhibition...","As a quasi-professional, Preston knew that losing this teamfight meant a guaranteed loss of his hundred million dollars.","\"Listen to me!\" Preston barked. \"I am going to win this exhibition! We are fighting to the death right here! If any of you die before Lawson does, I will see to it that one million dollars is deducted from your annual stipends!\"","Gritting his teeth, Preston commanded the charge into the neutral river territory.","His only imperative was to assassinate Jude’s marksman.","\"I don’t care how many defensive shields they stack!\" Preston yelled into his comms. \"Focus everything on Lawson! Kill the Core DPS! Even if we all wipe, I want to see his screen turn gray at least once!\"","As the Vanguard team breached the river, Preston hung back slightly, waiting for his frontline to absorb the initial wave of crowd control.","Before Preston could even activate his offensive cooldowns, his four teammates marched forward in a single-file line directly into the Apex artillery fire.","They walked into the center of Jude’s area-of-effect damage, absorbing maximum punishment until all four of their health bars hovered at a single pixel.","Sitting on his throne, Jude simply tapped his mouse button four distinct times.","[First Blood!]","[Double Kill!]","[Triple Kill!]","[Quadra Kill!]*","\"Boss, boss! You only need one more for the Server Wipe!\" the Apex Top-Laner screamed, mashing his keyboard.","\"Do not let the Vanguard heir escape! Trap him!\" the Support player roared. \"I’ll take point! I’m going to lock his character to the floor, whoever steals the boss’s final kill is dead to me!\"","Before Preston could even process the betrayal of his own roster, the entire Apex squad swarmed his position.","True to his word, the Apex Support flashed forward.","The rest of the team whittled Preston’s health down, pulling their punches at the exact last second to leave him wounded.","Jude navigated his champion forward with casual grace. Before he was even fully in range, he tossed out a single attack.","Preston watched as his screen faded to black.","[VICTORY!]","Jude leaned back in his chair, watching the Vanguard base explode into fragments.","[Corporate Dominance Task Completed!]","[Wager Secured: +$100,000,000 liquid capital.]","[Rewarding +2 Liquid Capital Sign-Ins, 1x High-Tier Corporate Asset Cache.]","Jude didn’t even care about the hundred-million-dollar wager he had just won from Preston; that was just petty cash.","What truly mattered was the cascading sequence of system injections preparing to flood his offshore portfolios!","[Executing Liquid Sign-In 1: +$150,000,000 successfully routed.]","[Executing Liquid Sign-In 2: +$210,000,000 successfully routed.]","In the span of five seconds, nearly four hundred million dollars materialized in Jude’s primary holding account.","Jude stood up, buttoning his jacket.","\"Gentlemen, an exceptional performance across the board,\" Jude announced. \"As promised, I have bought out Le Bernardin for the evening. We are celebrating this victory with a Michelin-starred banquet.\"","Jude then turned his gaze across the aisle toward the Vanguard side.","\"Furthermore,\" Jude added, a smile touching his lips. \"If there are any Vanguard athletes who are currently dissatisfied with their toxic management, you are more than welcome to join us for dinner. Apex Media has plenty of capital to go around.\"","As soon as Jude opened his mouth, the four Vanguard professionals immediately stood up, tearing off their jerseys..."]}]);
